              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "calculated",
            "name": "Expertise Role (All Cohorts)",
            "dataType": "string",
            "description": [
              "Expertise_Role for every cohort, with Cowork filled in from the material each prompt touched.",
              "",
              "WHY. The feed derives Expertise_Role from Behavior_Enriched_Full, which it derives from",
              "AccessedResource_Type matched against file extensions (xlsx, pdf, docx ...). Cowork logs MIME",
              "types instead (application/vnd...spreadsheetml.sheet, application/pdf ...), so none match, every",
              "Cowork row falls through to \"General Chat\" and Expertise_Role is blank for 100% of Cowork.",
              "",
              "RULE (Cowork only, per row): the feed's own resource rule, after translating MIME to extension.",
              "email item (rfc822, ms-outlook)   Executive Assistant (Communications Specialist if sent or drafted)",
              "chat message                      Collaboration Lead",
              "spreadsheet or CSV                Spreadsheet Specialist",
              "PDF                               Researcher",
              "HTML, JSON, XML, plain text       Software Engineer",
              "PNG, JPEG, GIF                    Visual Designer",
              "Word document                     Content Writer (Knowledge Navigator when only read)",
              "PowerPoint deck                   Presentation Designer (Knowledge Navigator when only read)",
              "anything else, or no material     blank, exactly as the feed leaves it",
              "Every other cohort gets Expertise_Role unchanged, row for row.",
              "",
              "LIMITS. It reads material, not intent, and inherits the feed's weak spots: plain text and HTML",
              "count as Software Engineer there too. The durable fix is upstream - normalise MIME types before",
              "the notebook's from_resource chain - after which this column can simply return Expertise_Role."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "IF(",
              "    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] <> \"Cowork\",",
              "    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Expertise_Role],",
              "    VAR _t = LOWER(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AccessedResource_Type]))",
              "    VAR _a = LOWER(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AccessedResource_Action]))",
              "    VAR _active =",
              "        CONTAINSSTRING(_a, \"send\") || CONTAINSSTRING(_a, \"draft\") || CONTAINSSTRING(_a, \"create\")",
              "            || CONTAINSSTRING(_a, \"post\") || CONTAINSSTRING(_a, \"invoke\") || CONTAINSSTRING(_a, \"write\")",
              "            || CONTAINSSTRING(_a, \"patch\") || CONTAINSSTRING(_a, \"execute\")",
              "    RETURN",
              "        SWITCH(",
              "            TRUE(),",
              "            _t IN { \"message/rfc822\", \"application/vnd.ms-outlook\" },",
              "                IF(_active, \"Communications Specialist\", \"Executive Assistant\"),",
              "            _t = \"message\",",
              "                \"Collaboration Lead\",",
              "            _t IN { \"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\", \"application/vnd.ms-excel\",",
              "                    \"application/vnd.ms-excel.sheet.macroenabled.12\", \"text/csv\" },",
              "                \"Spreadsheet Specialist\",",
              "            _t = \"application/pdf\",",
              "                \"Researcher\",",
              "            _t IN { \"application/json\", \"application/xml\", \"text/xml\", \"text/html\", \"text/plain\" },",
              "                \"Software Engineer\",",
              "            _t IN { \"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\", \"image/gif\" },",
              "                \"Visual Designer\",",
              "            _t IN { \"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\", \"application/msword\",",
              "                    \"application/rtf\" },",
              "                IF(NOT(_active) && _a = \"read\", \"Knowledge Navigator\", \"Content Writer\"),",
              "            _t IN { \"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation\",",
              "                    \"application/vnd.ms-powerpoint\" },",
              "                IF(NOT(_active) && _a = \"read\", \"Knowledge Navigator\", \"Presentation Designer\"),",
              "            BLANK()",
              "        )",
              ")"
            ],
            "lineageTag": "ff1e0001-0001-0001-0001-000000000001",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "SummarizationSetBy",
                "value": "Automatic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "calculated",
            "name": "Is Material Ref",
            "dataType": "boolean",
            "description": [
              "TRUE when this row points at real work material - a file, mail item, message, meeting or page -",
              "rather than a retrieval pointer. The one place the fit chain decides what counts as material.",
              "",
              "COWORK (unchanged rule): any typed resource except \"message\". Cowork logs MIME types and only",
              "typed material reaches the log, so the original test stands exactly. Its \"message\" rows are",
              "messages Cowork READ: not material, but counted as evidence by Session Message Reads.",
              "",
              "OTHER TOOLS (allow-list): Copilot and agents log extensions (docx, xlsx, pptx, pdf, EmailMessage,",
              "TeamsMessage, Event ...) AND retrieval pointers. CITATION (1.74M rows), HyperLink (1.45M),",
              "WebSearchQuery, RICHWEBANSWER, News, People, ufsFAQ and API are excluded: 60% of citing",
              "messages carry no typed file at all, so counting citations would grade answer formatting, not",
              "work. An allow-list keeps the rule a FLOOR, like the rest of the chain - an unknown type is",
              "never counted as material."
            ],
            "isHidden": true,
            "expression": [
              "VAR _raw = TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AccessedResource_Type])",
              "VAR _t = LOWER(_raw)",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\",",
              "        NOT ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AccessedResource_Type]) && LEN(_raw) > 0 && _t <> \"message\",",
              "        _t IN { \"docx\", \"doc\", \"xlsx\", \"xlsm\", \"xls\", \"csv\", \"pptx\", \"ppt\", \"pdf\", \"txt\", \"md\", \"html\", \"htm\", \"json\", \"xml\", \"py\", \"zip\", \"png\", \"jpg\", \"jpeg\", \"gif\", \"mp4\", \"loop\", \"aspx\", \"sitepagemodern\", \"onepart\", \"page\", \"eml\", \"msg\", \"emailmessage\", \"teamsmessage\", \"event\", \"file\", \"external\", \"report\" }",
              "    )"
            ],
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
            "summarizeBy": "none"
          },
          {
            "name": "Is Usage Row",
            "type": "calculated",
            "expression": "'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Prompt Row] || 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork]",
            "dataType": "boolean",
            "isHidden": true,
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "description": [
              "TRUE for rows that show a person used Copilot: every prompt row, plus",
              "Cowork task rows. Scheduled and autonomous Cowork runs carry no prompt,",
              "so the audit parsers keep each one as a single task row",
              "(Message_isPrompt = FALSE). Drives the active-user counts only; prompt,",
              "task and session measures stay prompt-based."
            ],
            "lineageTag": "81c56ca4-90a6-573b-85cf-0d5b9f8cdf17"
          }
        ],
        "partitions": [
          {
            "name": "Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)",
            "mode": "import",
            "source": {
              "type": "m",
              "expression": [
                "let",
                "    // Value Lens 2307 (Spark) update: audit-log shaping now happens once in Spark",
                "    // (notebook Copilot_Audit_Log_Processor -> Delta table copilot_interactions_curated).",
                "    // Thin, query-folding passthrough: a single CreationDate range filter that folds to the",
                "    // Lakehouse SQL endpoint so Incremental Refresh only touches new day-partitions",
                "    // (and the model is Direct Lake-ready). All 59 output columns come straight from Spark.",
                "    Source   = FabricTable(\"copilot_interactions_curated\"),",
                "    Filtered = Table.SelectRows(Source, each [CreationDate] >= RangeStart and [CreationDate] < RangeEnd),",
                "    // Drop columns no visual or measure reads. This folds to a SQL projection,",
                "    // and removes 444 MB of AccessedResource_SiteUrl from every refresh.",
                "    Trimmed = Table.RemoveColumns(Filtered, {\"AccessedResource_SiteUrl\", \"Delegation_Event_Key\", \"AccessedResource_SensitivityLabelId\", \"AISystemPlugin_Id\", \"AISystemPlugin_Name\", \"AppIdentity_AppId\", \"AppIdentity_DisplayName\", \"AppIdentity_PublisherId\", \"ApplicationName\", \"Audit_UserKey\", \"Agent_EntraId\", \"Agent_TitleID\", \"Agent Last Used Date\", \"ClientRegion\", \"Is_Sensitive\", \"ModelTransparencyDetails_ModelName\", \"ModelTransparencyDetails_ModelProviderName\", \"Web_Grounded_Signal\", \"Workload\", \"Has license\", \"SensitivityLabelId\", \"Behavior_Source\", \"Behavior_Enriched\", \"User_Stage\", \"UserMonthKey\", \"Resource_Count\", \"Grounding Source\", \"Agent_Surface\", \"Execution_Trigger\", \"AppIdentity_Text\", \"Agent_TargetPlatformId\", \"Agent_TargetName\", \"Agent_PlatformType\"}, MissingField.Ignore)",
                "in",
                "    Trimmed"
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "measures": [
          {
            "name": "Active Unlicensed Users",
            "description": "Users with prompt-flagged audit activity in the selected Unlicensed cohort.",
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: distinct counts of the IDs with usage rows, less any blank or",
              "// whitespace-only IDs, instead of one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId",
              "// is filtered directly (user rows, a user slicer, or a selection that pairs",
              "// users with other fields) the per-user form runs, so results always match it.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([Usage Rows]) > 0)),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\")",
              "    ),",
              "    VAR BlankIds =",
              "        FILTER(",
              "            ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) = 0",
              "        )",
              "    VAR UsageIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\")",
              "        )",
              "    VAR BlankUsageIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS(BlankIds)",
              "        )",
              "    VAR ActiveIds = UsageIds - BlankUsageIds",
              "    RETURN",
              "        IF(ActiveIds > 0, ActiveIds)",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Unlicensed - Value",
            "lineageTag": "385c52b8-89d9-454b-b37e-1a90dd3b5038",
            "changedProperties": [
              {
                "property": "IsHidden"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Active Licensed Users",
            "description": "Users with prompt-flagged audit activity in the selected Licensed cohort.",
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: distinct counts of the IDs with usage rows, less any blank or",
              "// whitespace-only IDs, instead of one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId",
              "// is filtered directly (user rows, a user slicer, or a selection that pairs",
              "// users with other fields) the per-user form runs, so results always match it.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([Usage Rows]) > 0)),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"M365 Copilot Licensed\")",
              "    ),",
              "    VAR BlankIds =",
              "        FILTER(",
              "            ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) = 0",
              "        )",
              "    VAR UsageIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"M365 Copilot Licensed\")",
              "        )",
              "    VAR BlankUsageIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"M365 Copilot Licensed\"),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS(BlankIds)",
              "        )",
              "    VAR ActiveIds = UsageIds - BlankUsageIds",
              "    RETURN",
              "        IF(ActiveIds > 0, ActiveIds)",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Licensed - Value",
            "lineageTag": "5ae3fdae-2e6a-432c-830d-841f1fd27c01"
          },
          {
            "name": "Most Versatile Agent",
            "description": [
              "User using most different agents",
              "🌟 Power user exploring broadly",
              "💡 Early adopter of new agents"
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "VAR AgentUserCounts = ",
              "    ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "        SUMMARIZE(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)',",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentName]",
              "        ),",
              "        \"@UniqueUsers\", ",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            NOT(ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentId]))",
              "        )",
              "    )",
              "VAR MaxUsers = MAXX(AgentUserCounts, [@UniqueUsers])",
              "VAR MostVersatile = ",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        AgentUserCounts,",
              "        [@UniqueUsers] = MaxUsers",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    CONCATENATEX(MostVersatile, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentName], \", \")"
            ],
            "lineageTag": "3673341d-b0ab-42fe-9efa-06440654aa0a"
          },
          {
            "name": "Most Popular Agent",
            "description": [
              "Most used agent by sessions",
              "🏆 Your champion agent",
              "💡 Study for success patterns"
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "-- Lists the agent(s) behind the activity in the current cell.",
              "-- Identity per row: AgentName when present, else AppHost",
              "-- (e.g. \"Logic App\", \"Autonomous\", \"Excel\") so Workflow Automation",
              "-- rows that have no AgentName still surface a meaningful identifier.",
              "-- Top 3 by row count, comma-joined; suffix \" +N more\" if there's a tail.",
              "VAR Tagged =",
              "    SELECTCOLUMNS(",
              "        FILTER(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)',",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "            && 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Agent_Activity] = TRUE()",
              "        ),",
              "        \"@Identity\",",
              "            IF(",
              "                NOT(ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentName]))",
              "                    && 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentName] <> \"\",",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentName],",
              "                COALESCE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost], \"Unknown\")",
              "            )",
              "    )",
              "VAR IdentityCounts =",
              "    GROUPBY(",
              "        Tagged,",
              "        [@Identity],",
              "        \"@Rows\", COUNTX(CURRENTGROUP(), 1)",
              "    )",
              "VAR TotalIdentities = COUNTROWS(IdentityCounts)",
              "VAR Top3 = TOPN(3, IdentityCounts, [@Rows], DESC)",
              "VAR Names = CONCATENATEX(Top3, [@Identity], \", \", [@Rows], DESC)",
              "VAR Remainder = TotalIdentities - 3",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(ISBLANK(TotalIdentities) || TotalIdentities = 0,",
              "        BLANK(),",
              "        Names & IF(Remainder > 0, \" +\" & FORMAT(Remainder, \"0\") & \" more\", \"\")",
              "    )"
            ],
            "lineageTag": "2fcb35a1-90b3-47bf-bc41-4103a2ab5069"
          },
          {
            "name": "Average Active Days Per User (Chat + Agents)",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "    )",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "lineageTag": "d80d3423-70f7-4dc3-9dcb-1d3d31e2fc2e",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "PBI_FormatHint",
                "value": "{\"isGeneralNumber\":true}"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "License Priority Score (User)",
            "description": [
              "=============================================================================",
              "LICENSE PRIORITY v2 (17 May 2026)",
              "",
              "Simple 2-signal score for ranking unlicensed users as Copilot license",
              "candidates. Each signal is normalised to a clear benchmark, capped at 1,",
              "then weighted to a 0-100 scale that maps cleanly onto action tiers.",
              "",
              "How much (60%) — Median Unlicensed AI Tasks per User per Week",
              "(full marks = 30 tasks/week, i.e. ~6 per workday)",
              "How often (40%) — Median Active Days per User per Week (Unlicensed)",
              "(full marks = 5 days/week, i.e. every working day)",
              "",
              "Score ≥ 70 → 🟢 Ready Now      | 50–69 → 🟡 Strong Candidate",
              "Score 30–49 → 🟠 Watch         | <30   → 🔴 Not Ready",
              "",
              "Confidence flag (High / Medium / Low) reflects weeks of data behind the",
              "score — stops one-good-week wonders outranking steady users.",
              "",
              "Previous sessions-based formula preserved as License Priority Score",
              "(User) [v1 Legacy] for back-compat with pre-existing visuals/bookmarks.",
              "=============================================================================",
              "License recommendation score (0-100). Higher = stronger license candidate."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR TasksPW = [Median Unlicensed AI Tasks Per User Per Week]",
              "VAR DaysPW  = [Median Chat + Agent Active Days Per User Per Week (Unlicensed)]",
              "VAR VolumeScore = MIN(DIVIDE(TasksPW, 30, 0), 1)",
              "VAR DaysScore   = MIN(DIVIDE(DaysPW,  5, 0), 1)",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        TasksPW <= 0 || DaysPW <= 0,",
              "        BLANK(),",
              "        ROUND(60 * VolumeScore + 40 * DaysScore, 0)",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "ce411199-5b7e-4555-bdaf-dd5d6c00aa3e",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "PBI_FormatHint",
                "value": "{\"isGeneralNumber\":true}"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Average Agent Sessions Per Active Agent User",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            NOT(ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentId]))",
              "        ) > 0",
              "    ),",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "        NOT(ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentId]))",
              "    )",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "lineageTag": "6e9306c6-0ddf-4b97-9729-909c8ad4cdaf"
          },
          {
            "name": "Average Chat Sessions Per User Per Week (All Licenses)",
            "description": [
              "Weekly avg sessions per user",
              "✅ >5/week = engaged",
              "⚠️ <2/week = at risk",
              "💡 Weekly habit indicator"
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    VAR TotalSessions =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    VAR TotalWeeks =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        DIVIDE(TotalSessions, TotalWeeks, 0)",
              ")",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "lineageTag": "7dcf5848-cc04-430b-b0ab-a7fbbe86419e",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "PBI_FormatHint",
                "value": "{\"isGeneralNumber\":true}"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Average Active Days Per User Per Week (Unlicensed Chat)",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"",
              "        ) > 0",
              "    ),",
              "    VAR TotalActiveDays =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    VAR TotalWeeks =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        DIVIDE(TotalActiveDays, TotalWeeks, 0)",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "lineageTag": "f88bd7cb-92b2-4d8c-8888-715c1a3705a6"
          },
          {
            "name": "Median Chat + Agent Active Days Per User Per Week (Unlicensed)",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "MEDIANX(",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"",
              "        ) > 0",
              "    ),",
              "    VAR TotalActiveDays =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    VAR TotalWeeks =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        DIVIDE(TotalActiveDays, TotalWeeks, 0)",
              ")",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "lineageTag": "b0ff8ef0-1b72-4efb-8d69-2ccd2b36a8eb"
          },
          {
            "name": "License Priority Rank (Dynamic)",
            "description": [
              "Dynamic ranking with current filters",
              "📊 Updates with your selections",
              "💡 Drill to see specific cohorts"
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "VAR CurrentScore = [License Priority Score (User)]",
              "VAR IsUserLevel = ISINSCOPE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])",
              "",
              "RETURN",
              "IF(",
              "    ISBLANK(CurrentScore),",
              "    BLANK(),",
              "    IF(",
              "        IsUserLevel,",
              "        // Rank users - ONLY those with unlicensed activity",
              "        RANKX(",
              "            FILTER(",
              "                ALLSELECTED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                CALCULATE(",
              "                    COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"",
              "                ) > 0",
              "                && NOT(ISBLANK([License Priority Score (User)]))",
              "            ),",
              "            [License Priority Score (User)],",
              "            ,",
              "            DESC,",
              "            DENSE",
              "        ),",
              "        // Rank organizations - ONLY those with unlicensed users",
              "        RANKX(",
              "            FILTER(",
              "                ALLSELECTED('Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization]),",
              "                CALCULATE(",
              "                    COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"",
              "                ) > 0",
              "                && NOT(ISBLANK([License Priority Score (User)]))",
              "            ),",
              "            [License Priority Score (User)],",
              "            ,",
              "            DESC,",
              "            DENSE",
              "        )",
              "    )",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0",
            "lineageTag": "d45ae6e2-c85c-41ff-99dc-7c4e4065c514"
          },
          {
            "name": "AI Tasks",
            "description": "Prompt-flagged curated audit activity rows. A task proxy, not an independently verified completed output; can differ from distinct prompts when curation expands activity.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'), KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Prompt Row] = TRUE()))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Value Types",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000047"
          },
          {
            "name": "Active Agent Users",
            "description": [
              "Users with prompt-flagged audit activity in the selected Agent cohort. Cowork is a",
              "separate AppHost-based cohort."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: distinct counts of the IDs with prompt rows, less any blank or",
              "// whitespace-only IDs, instead of one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId",
              "// is filtered directly (user rows, a user slicer, or a selection that pairs",
              "// users with other fields) the per-user form runs, so results always match it.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([AI Tasks]) > 0)),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Agents\")",
              "    ),",
              "    VAR BlankIds =",
              "        FILTER(",
              "            ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) = 0",
              "        )",
              "    VAR PromptIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Prompt Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Agents\")",
              "        )",
              "    VAR BlankPromptIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Prompt Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Agents\"),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS(BlankIds)",
              "        )",
              "    VAR ActiveIds = PromptIds - BlankPromptIds",
              "    RETURN",
              "        IF(ActiveIds > 0, ActiveIds)",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000153"
          },
          {
            "name": "All Active Users",
            "description": "Nonblank users with prompt-flagged activity in the selected scope.",
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: distinct counts of the IDs with usage rows, less any blank or",
              "// whitespace-only IDs, instead of one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId",
              "// is filtered directly (user rows, a user slicer, or a selection that pairs",
              "// users with other fields) the per-user form runs, so results always match it.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    COUNTROWS(FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([Usage Rows]) > 0)),",
              "    VAR BlankIds =",
              "        FILTER(",
              "            ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) = 0",
              "        )",
              "    VAR UsageIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE())",
              "        )",
              "    VAR BlankUsageIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS(BlankIds)",
              "        )",
              "    VAR ActiveIds = UsageIds - BlankUsageIds",
              "    RETURN",
              "        IF(ActiveIds > 0, ActiveIds)",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "ff020001-0001-0001-0001-000000000204"
          },
          {
            "name": "Stage Top Org",
            "description": [
              "=============================================================================",
              "Stage Profile: Top org for current stage context"
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR OrgTable =",
              "    ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization]),",
              "        \"UserCount\",",
              "        CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]))",
              "    )",
              "VAR TopRow = TOPN(1, OrgTable, [UserCount], DESC)",
              "RETURN MAXX(TopRow, 'Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization])"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Stage Profiles",
            "lineageTag": "ff020001-0001-0001-0001-000000000602"
          },
          {
            "name": "Expert Equivalent Hours",
            "description": [
              "Total human-equivalent hours: what AI is handling that humans would otherwise do.",
              "Cowork is priced from its v4 task category, everything else from its behaviour.",
              "The split exists because Cowork carries no behaviour detail - the feed tags all of",
              "it \"General Chat\", the map's explicit no-signals-matched fallback - so pricing it",
              "on the behaviour basis valued the premium surface at the lowest band published."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    [Human Equivalent Hours (Behaviour Basis)],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] <> \"Cowork\")",
              ") + [Cowork Hours (Task Category Basis)]"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Time Savings",
            "lineageTag": "fc000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000005"
          },
          {
            "name": "Avg Skills Per User",
            "description": [
              "Average augmented skills per user",
              "Distinct kinds of work per user - the breadth half of AI fluency.",
              "Counts Task Breakdown Category, NOT Behavior_Category. The Fabric feed",
              "gives every Cowork row one behaviour, so on Behavior_Category this",
              "measure returned exactly 1.000 for every Cowork user - a statement",
              "about the feed, not the estate. Task Breakdown Category substitutes",
              "only for Cowork, so Copilot (7.228) and Agents (4.174) are unchanged",
              "while Cowork moves 1.000 -> 3.016."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    AVERAGEX(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Task Breakdown Category]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "        )",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Augmented Skills",
            "lineageTag": "ff080001-0001-0001-0001-000000000014"
          },
          {
            "name": "Expert Equivalent Hours Per User",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    DIVIDE(",
              "        [Expert Equivalent Hours],",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        0",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Time Savings",
            "lineageTag": "f6e1f84b-1a34-4bc7-b296-c5a585fba0ad",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "PBI_FormatHint",
                "value": "{\"isGeneralNumber\":true}"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Mode Share",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    DIVIDE(",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "        ),",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Task Engagement Mode]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Usage_Mode])",
              "        ),",
              "        0",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.00%;-0.00%;0.00%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Usage Modes",
            "lineageTag": "31b0953a-8e21-43c7-9609-9bd33c63ec8a"
          },
          {
            "name": "% of Users in Stage",
            "description": "% of users in current stage leveraging this Usage Mode, Behavior, or Breakdown (works at all drill levels)",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    VAR UsersInContext =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "        )",
              "    VAR TotalUsersInStage =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Usage_Mode]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Behavior_Enriched_Full]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Behavior_Category]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Value_Outcome]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Efficiency_Breakdown]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Expertise_Role]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Expertise Role (All Cohorts)])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN DIVIDE(UsersInContext, TotalUsersInStage, 0)"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Usage Modes",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000029"
          },
          {
            "name": "New Expertise - Users",
            "description": "Users accessing specialist capabilities",
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "    NOT(ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Expertise Role (All Cohorts)]))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\4 - New Expertise",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000115"
          },
          {
            "name": "Efficiency - Hours Per User Per Week",
            "description": "Expert Equivalent Hours per active user per active week",
            "expression": [
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), ALLEXCEPT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)', 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), VALUES('Calendar'[Date])),",
              "    DIVIDE([Expert Equivalent Hours], DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]), 0)",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "isHidden": true,
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\1 - Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000101"
          },
          {
            "name": "Expert Equivalent Hours Per Week",
            "description": [
              "Expert Equivalent Hours delivered per calendar week (org total). No reinvestment or",
              "realisation discount is applied - this is the full estimated expert effort."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Expert Equivalent Hours], CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), ALLEXCEPT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)', 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), VALUES('Calendar'[Date])), 0)",
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Time Savings",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000102"
          },
          {
            "name": "Work Created - Per Week",
            "description": "Work items created per week (org total)",
            "expression": [
              "DIVIDE(",
              "    CALCULATE(COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Usage_Mode] IN {\"4 - Producing\"}),",
              "    CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), ALLEXCEPT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)', 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), VALUES('Calendar'[Date])),",
              "    0",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\2 - Work Created",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000106"
          },
          {
            "name": "New Expertise - Roles",
            "description": "Specialist roles active",
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Expertise Role (All Cohorts)]),",
              "    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "    NOT(ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Expertise Role (All Cohorts)]))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\4 - New Expertise",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000114"
          },
          {
            "name": "Agent AI Tasks",
            "description": "AI task proxy rows in the Agent cohort; same base activity definition as AI Tasks.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([AI Tasks], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Agents\"))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Agent - Value",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000139"
          },
          {
            "name": "Copilot AI Tasks",
            "description": "AI task proxy rows in the Licensed cohort; same base activity definition as AI Tasks.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([AI Tasks], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"M365 Copilot Licensed\"))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Licensed - Value",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000154"
          },
          {
            "name": "Unlicensed AI Tasks",
            "description": "AI task proxy rows in the Unlicensed cohort; same base activity definition as AI Tasks.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([AI Tasks], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Unlicensed - Value",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000164"
          },
          {
            "name": "AI Assisted Value",
            "description": [
              "AI Assisted Value: Hours x Hourly Value x Penalty Factor (all adjustable via slicers).",
              "Uses the full human-equivalent hours; no reinvestment haircut is applied to the value calculation.",
              "Returns BLANK when the Hourly Value box is left empty (no default rate is assumed)."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    IF(",
              "        ISBLANK(SELECTEDVALUE('Hourly Value'[Hourly Value])),",
              "        BLANK(),",
              "        [Expert Equivalent Hours]",
              "        * [Hourly Value Value]",
              "        * [Penalty Factor Value]",
              "    )",
              ""
            ],
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\ROI",
            "lineageTag": "ff0b0001-0001-0001-0001-000000000020",
            "formatStringDefinition": {
              "expression": "\"\"\"\" & [Currency Symbol Value] & \"\"\"#,##0\""
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Copilot License Investment",
            "description": "Copilot License Investment: PPUPM x Licensed Users x Months (fixed cost regardless of filter)",
            "expression": [
              "SUMX(",
              "    VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart]),",
              "    [AI PPUPM Value] *",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"M365 Copilot Licensed\"",
              "    )",
              ")"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\ROI",
            "lineageTag": "ff0b0001-0001-0001-0001-000000000022",
            "formatStringDefinition": {
              "expression": "\"\"\"\" & [Currency Symbol Value] & \"\"\"#,##0\""
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Top Value Outcome",
            "description": "Top Value Outcome by expert equivalent hours (dynamic to filters). When the filter context holds only Cowork activity it ranks Cowork Task Category instead: every Cowork row is classed General Chat, so Value_Outcome cannot tell Cowork tasks apart, and this keeps the Cowork card in line with the Cowork task breakdown. Mixed and non-Cowork contexts are unchanged.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _hasNonCowork =",
              "    NOT ISEMPTY(",
              "        CALCULATETABLE(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)',",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] <> \"Cowork\")",
              "        )",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        _hasNonCowork,",
              "        MAXX(",
              "            TOPN(1,",
              "                ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "                    VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Value_Outcome]),",
              "                    \"@Hrs\", [Expert Equivalent Hours]",
              "                ),",
              "                [@Hrs], DESC",
              "            ),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Value_Outcome]",
              "        ),",
              "        MAXX(",
              "            TOPN(1,",
              "                ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "                    FILTER(",
              "                        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category]),",
              "                        NOT ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category])",
              "                    ),",
              "                    \"@Hrs\", [Expert Equivalent Hours]",
              "                ),",
              "                [@Hrs], DESC",
              "            ),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category]",
              "        )",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\1 - Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff030001-0001-0001-0001-000000000175"
          },
          {
            "name": "AI Assisted Value Per Week",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "IF(",
              "    ISBLANK([AI Assisted Value]),",
              "    BLANK(),",
              "    DIVIDE(",
              "        [AI Assisted Value],",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]),",
              "        0",
              "    )",
              ")"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\ROI",
            "lineageTag": "2769b48a-57a1-4acb-8a8b-6e3d70626ad7",
            "formatStringDefinition": {
              "expression": "\"\"\"\" & [Currency Symbol Value] & \"\"\"#,##0\""
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Projected Annualised Value",
            "description": "Projected annualised value at current adoption (observed value scaled from visible weeks to 52)",
            "expression": [
              "VAR WeeksInView = DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "VAR AnnualFactor = DIVIDE(52, MAX(WeeksInView, 1), 0)",
              "RETURN [AI Assisted Value] * AnnualFactor"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Functional Value",
            "lineageTag": "ff0c0001-0001-0001-0001-000000000044",
            "formatStringDefinition": {
              "expression": "\"\"\"\" & [Currency Symbol Value] & \"\"\"#,##0\""
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Net ROI",
            "description": [
              "Net ROI: AI Assisted Value minus Copilot License Investment (benefit after licence cost,",
              "shown in the Assumptions[Currency Symbol Value] currency).",
              "How to read: positive and growing is the goal. At or near zero, measured value is only covering licence spend; negative means spend currently exceeds measured value."
            ],
            "expression": "[AI Assisted Value] - [Copilot License Investment]",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\ROI",
            "lineageTag": "ff0b0001-0001-0001-0001-000000000031",
            "formatStringDefinition": {
              "expression": "\"\"\"\" & [Currency Symbol Value] & \"\"\"#,##0\""
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Activity Share",
            "description": [
              "Activity Share: this prompt count ÷ all prompts in the current OUTSIDE filter",
              "context (Date, Org, License, Agent slicers etc.) but ignoring whatever",
              "dimension is being charted inside the visual.",
              "",
              "Uses ALLSELECTED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)') so it is robust",
              "when ANY column from that table is dropped onto a visual's Axis, Legend or",
              "Detail bucket — including Behavior_Enriched_Full, Workflow_Action,",
              "Usage_Mode, Value_Outcome, Expertise_Role, Efficiency_Breakdown, etc.",
              "",
              "Previously hand-maintained REMOVEFILTERS column list silently broke when",
              "a new dimension (e.g., Workflow_Action) was added as a treemap Detail —",
              "the denominator was no longer the global total, causing parent rectangles",
              "to double in size. ALLSELECTED removes the maintenance burden."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    DIVIDE(",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "        ),",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            ALLSELECTED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)')",
              "        ),",
              "        0",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.00%;-0.00%;0.00%",
            "lineageTag": "be5a75f5-b45a-4db7-a70f-8f67dd6ba89f"
          },
          {
            "name": "Activation Overall Headline",
            "description": "Current activity counts without unsupported claims about adoption growth or purchase readiness.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _Active = COALESCE([All Active Users],0)",
              "VAR _Total = [Total Users (Filter-Aware)]",
              "RETURN FORMAT(_Active,\"#,##0\") & \" active users\"",
              "    & IF(_Total >= _Active && _Total > 0, \" of \" & FORMAT(_Total,\"#,##0\") & \" roster users\", \"\")",
              "    & \" | \" & FORMAT(COALESCE([Active Licensed Users],0),\"#,##0\") & \" licensed, \"",
              "    & FORMAT(COALESCE([Active Unlicensed Users],0),\"#,##0\") & \" unlicensed observed in audit.\""
            ],
            "formatString": "@",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "6e6e8ed5-f2cf-4aea-b6e9-f55166eb485d"
          },
          {
            "name": "Activation Licensed Headline",
            "description": "Evidence-based activation summary that surfaces mismatched inventories instead of zero utilization.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _Active = COALESCE([Active Licensed Users],0)",
              "VAR _Total = [Licensed Users (Filter-Aware)]",
              "RETURN IF(ISBLANK(_Total) || _Active > _Total,",
              "    FORMAT(_Active,\"#,##0\") & \" licensed users observed. License inventory does not reconcile; utilization is unavailable.\",",
              "    FORMAT(_Active,\"#,##0\") & \" of \" & FORMAT(_Total,\"#,##0\")",
              "        & \" matched license holders active (\" & FORMAT(DIVIDE(_Active,_Total),\"0.0%\") & \").\")"
            ],
            "formatString": "@",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "f02132e8-6d82-4d8e-9c9d-0bceb2a88d42"
          },
          {
            "name": "Activation Unlicensed Headline",
            "description": "Observed usage is not a ready-to-convert or entitlement determination.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _Active = COALESCE([Active Unlicensed Users],0)",
              "VAR _Total = [Unlicensed Users (Filter-Aware)]",
              "RETURN FORMAT(_Active,\"#,##0\") & \" unlicensed users observed.\"",
              "    & IF(ISBLANK(_Total) || _Active > _Total,",
              "        \" Population share unavailable: license inventory does not reconcile.\",",
              "        \" \" & FORMAT(DIVIDE(_Active,_Total),\"0.0%\") & \" of the matched unlicensed population.\")",
              "    & \" Usage alone does not establish a need for a paid license.\""
            ],
            "formatString": "@",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "b055f7f7-74ba-403f-8e0b-eba03c113e69"
          },
          {
            "name": "Activation Agents Headline",
            "description": "Observed agent footprint; no growth inference from a single current-period share.",
            "expression": [
              "FORMAT(COALESCE([Active Agent Users],0),\"#,##0\") & \" users with observed agent activity\"",
              "    & \" | \" & FORMAT([Observed Agent Sessions],\"#,##0\") & \" sessions in this selection.\"",
              "    & \" Cowork activity is shown separately.\""
            ],
            "formatString": "@",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "379b329c-a2fe-4612-976c-bbc08eb5cd90"
          },
          {
            "name": "Inactive Users (Filter-Aware)",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    MAX(0, [Total Users (Filter-Aware)] - [All Active Users])",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0",
            "lineageTag": "b002ee7e-743a-4a71-b070-3ca21a91df78"
          },
          {
            "name": "% of Users by Activity",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    VAR ActStatus = SELECTEDVALUE('Activity (Legend)'[Value1])",
              "    VAR Denom = [Total Users (Filter-Aware)]",
              "    RETURN",
              "        SWITCH(",
              "            ActStatus,",
              "            \"Total Active\",   DIVIDE([All Active Users],   Denom, 0),",
              "            \"Total Inactive\", DIVIDE([Inactive Users (Filter-Aware)], Denom, 0),",
              "            DIVIDE([Total Users (Filter-Aware)], Denom, 0)",
              "        )",
              ""
            ],
            "lineageTag": "3de402e0-5577-4e69-ae80-7f67c5ef1efe",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "PBI_FormatHint",
                "value": "{\"isGeneralNumber\":true}"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Expert Equivalent Hours Per Active User",
            "description": [
              "Total human-equivalent hours delivered divided by distinct active users.",
              "Undiscounted - no reinvestment or realisation factor is applied."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    DIVIDE(",
              "        [Expert Equivalent Hours],",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        0",
              "    )",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "isHidden": true,
            "lineageTag": "0b01dc57-761a-45f4-be02-5d05f491f11c",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "PBI_FormatHint",
                "value": "{\"isGeneralNumber\":true}"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Habitual Users",
            "description": [
              "Habitual Users: 11-15 active days in the latest",
              "rolling 4-week window. Embedded across the week."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR CurrentWeek = MAX('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "VAR WindowStart = CurrentWeek - 21",
              "VAR UserStats =",
              "    ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "        CALCULATETABLE(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] >= WindowStart,",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] <= CurrentWeek",
              "        ),",
              "        \"Behaviors\",  CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Behavior_Enriched_Full]), REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] >= WindowStart, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] <= CurrentWeek),",
              "        \"ActiveDays\", CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),         REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] >= WindowStart, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] <= CurrentWeek)",
              "    )",
              "RETURN COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserStats, [ActiveDays] >= 11 && [ActiveDays] <= 15))"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\User Stages",
            "lineageTag": "ff020001-0001-0001-0001-000000000303"
          },
          {
            "name": "Power Users",
            "description": [
              "Power Users: 16+ active days",
              "— all measured over the latest rolling 4-week window. Champion cohort."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR CurrentWeek = MAX('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "VAR WindowStart = CurrentWeek - 21",
              "VAR UserStats =",
              "    ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "        CALCULATETABLE(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] >= WindowStart,",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] <= CurrentWeek",
              "        ),",
              "        \"ActiveDays\", CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),         REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] >= WindowStart, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] <= CurrentWeek),",
              "        \"ValueShare\", DIVIDE(",
              "            CALCULATE(COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'), REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Usage_Mode] = \"4 - Producing\", 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] >= WindowStart, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] <= CurrentWeek),",
              "            CALCULATE(COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'), REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] >= WindowStart, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] <= CurrentWeek),",
              "            0",
              "        ),",
              "        \"HasAgent\",   CALCULATE(COUNTROWS(FILTER('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)', NOT(ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentName])) && 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AgentName] <> \"\")), REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] >= WindowStart, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart] <= CurrentWeek) > 0",
              "    )",
              "RETURN COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserStats,",
              "    [ActiveDays] >= 16",
              "))"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\User Stages",
            "lineageTag": "ff020001-0001-0001-0001-000000000304"
          },
          {
            "name": "Habitual + Power %",
            "description": [
              "Habit + Power combined % — % of active users at the top 2 maturity stages",
              "How to read: the share of active users who reached the top two maturity stages. Rising over time is the goal; compare orgs using the Internal Benchmark rather than a fixed target."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Habitual Users] + [Power Users], [All Active Users], 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\User Stages",
            "lineageTag": "ff020001-0001-0001-0001-000000000311"
          },
          {
            "name": "Median Unlicensed AI Tasks Per User Per Week",
            "description": [
              "Median weekly AI Tasks per unlicensed user — count of prompt rows submitted",
              "per user, averaged across weeks they were active, then taken at the median.",
              "Powers the volume signal in License Priority Score (User) v2. Uses the same",
              "\"Tasks Performed\" definition (Message_isPrompt = TRUE) as the rest of the",
              "report — consistent with the Activity & Value page and Executive Headline."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "MEDIANX(",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"",
              "        ) > 0",
              "    ),",
              "    VAR TotalTasks =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    VAR TotalWeeks =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\",",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        DIVIDE(TotalTasks, TotalWeeks, 0)",
              ")",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "ce411199-5b7e-4555-bdaf-dd5d6c00ab04"
          },
          {
            "name": "AI Tasks per Active User",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "DIVIDE(",
              "    [AI Tasks],",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "    ),",
              "    0",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "lineageTag": "a0ebd5be-5714-4c36-918c-474bf2a1a63f"
          },
          {
            "name": "Heatmap Headline",
            "description": "Headline follows the same field parameter as the heatmap, including observed Sessions.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _Order = SELECTEDVALUE('Heatmap Toggle'[Heatmap Toggle Order], 0)",
              "VAR _Metric = SWITCH(_Order, 0, \"Active Users\", 1, \"Active Days / User\",",
              "    3, \"Modeled Hours / User\", 4, \"Sessions / User\")",
              "VAR _Ranked = ADDCOLUMNS(VALUES('Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization]),",
              "    \"@Value\", SWITCH(_Order, 0, [All Active Users], 1, [Average Active Days Per User (Chat + Agents)],",
              "        3, [Expert Equivalent Hours Per Active User], 4, [Observed Sessions per User]))",
              "VAR _Active = FILTER(_Ranked, [@Value] > 0)",
              "VAR _Lead = TOPN(1, _Active, [@Value], DESC, 'Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization], ASC)",
              "VAR _Fmt = IF(_Order = 0, \"#,##0\", \"#,##0.0\")",
              "RETURN IF(COUNTROWS(_Active) = 0, \"No activity in the current selection.\",",
              "    _Metric & \": \" & MAXX(_Lead, 'Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization])",
              "        & \" leads at \" & FORMAT(MAXX(_Lead, [@Value]), _Fmt)",
              "        & \" across \" & FORMAT(COUNTROWS(_Active),\"#,##0\") & \" active teams.\")"
            ],
            "formatString": "@",
            "displayFolder": "Heatmap",
            "lineageTag": "7912b8e2-8aad-4797-b568-bdaf864728fb"
          },
          {
            "name": "Habitual Users %",
            "description": [
              "Share of all active users in the Habitual band (11-15 active days) over the latest",
              "rolling 4-week window. Respects all page slicers."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Habitual Users], [All Active Users], 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\User Stages",
            "lineageTag": "b4fbd688-ea47-41d1-9053-9d7d332b5757"
          },
          {
            "name": "Last Full Month Start",
            "description": [
              "Helper - first day of the month the Habit Formation stages are placed on: the latest",
              "month the selected dates reach, capped at the last COMPLETE calendar month in the data.",
              "If the latest interaction date is the last day of its month, that month counts as",
              "complete; otherwise the previous month is used. Blank when the selected dates hold no",
              "complete month. Hidden; drives all 'Last Month' measures so a part-month is never",
              "reported as if it were whole."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR MaxDate =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        MAX('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "        ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "        ALL('Calendar')",
              "    )",
              "VAR IsComplete = MaxDate = EOMONTH(MaxDate, 0)",
              "VAR LastFull = IF(IsComplete, EOMONTH(MaxDate, -1) + 1, EOMONTH(MaxDate, -2) + 1)",
              "// The date slicer: the month holding the last selected date, never later than",
              "// LastFull, and nothing when every selected date falls after LastFull.",
              "VAR SelFirst = MIN('Calendar'[Date])",
              "VAR SelMonth = EOMONTH(MAX('Calendar'[Date]), -1) + 1",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        SelFirst <= EOMONTH(LastFull, 0),",
              "        IF(SelMonth < LastFull, SelMonth, LastFull)",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "General Date",
            "isHidden": true,
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "5fd9b5b4-930c-4d1d-b1c8-56ff39f8aeb7"
          },
          {
            "name": "Active Users, Last Month",
            "description": [
              "Distinct users with any activity in the last complete calendar month. Respects the",
              "Environment / Agent Filter / Organization slicers."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR MStart = [Last Full Month Start]",
              "RETURN",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "4a3b26fd-6e8b-4b5c-8976-41b49a2b2ce5"
          },
          {
            "name": "Inactive Users, Last Month",
            "description": [
              "Licensed users with ZERO activity in the month the Habit Formation stages are placed",
              "on (see Last Full Month Start). ORG-AWARE via TREATAS so an organization slicer",
              "filters the licensed base as well as the active side.",
              "Blank under an Agents, Cowork or Unlicensed selection - only Copilot has a seat",
              "inventory, so there is no licensed base to be inactive against. The card reads N/A,",
              "and Stage Base then falls back to the active users alone."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Inactive = holds a Copilot seat but did not use it. Only Copilot has a seat",
              "// list, so the Activity and License slicers (page filters on the audit fact",
              "// table) leave LicensedInScope at the full seat count while the active side",
              "// shrinks to Agents, Cowork or Unlicensed activity - subtracting two different",
              "// populations (measured 11,442 - 183 = 11,316 against 186 observed Cowork",
              "// users). Report nothing rather than a number that cannot be sourced.",
              "VAR Activity = SELECTEDVALUE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)], \"\")",
              "VAR Licence = SELECTEDVALUE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Environment], \"\")",
              "VAR Measured = NOT (Activity IN {\"Agents\", \"Cowork\"}) && Licence <> \"Unlicensed\"",
              "VAR MStart = [Last Full Month Start]",
              "VAR LicensedInScope =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        [Total Licensed Users],",
              "        TREATAS(VALUES('Chat + Agent Org Data'[PersonId]), 'Copilot Licensed'[UPN_Normalized])",
              "    )",
              "VAR LicensedActive =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        [Active Licensed Users],",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        Measured && NOT ISBLANK(MStart),",
              "        MAX(LicensedInScope - LicensedActive, 0)",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "d68d8587-b2c5-48ae-8ca3-4a6d2b7016fa"
          },
          {
            "name": "Beginner Users, Last Month",
            "description": [
              "Users with 1-5 active days in the last complete calendar month. Computed from the",
              "fact table, so it responds to the Environment / Agent Filter / Organization slicers."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one SUMMARIZECOLUMNS counts every user's active days, instead of",
              "// one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a",
              "// user slicer, or a selection that pairs users with other fields) the per-user",
              "// form runs, so results always match it. Needs the June 2024 or later engine.",
              "VAR MStart = [Last Full Month Start]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        VAR UserDays =",
              "            ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "                CALCULATETABLE(",
              "                    VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                    REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "                ),",
              "                \"Days\",",
              "                    CALCULATE(",
              "                        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "                        REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "                    )",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 1 && [Days] <= 5)),",
              "        VAR UserDays =",
              "            CALCULATETABLE(",
              "                SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "                    \"Days\", DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "                ),",
              "                REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 1 && [Days] <= 5))",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "ee75c293-adba-4df4-a626-6558fff90aca"
          },
          {
            "name": "Developing Users, Last Month",
            "description": "Users with 6-10 active days in the last complete calendar month. Slicer-responsive.",
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one SUMMARIZECOLUMNS counts every user's active days, instead of",
              "// one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a",
              "// user slicer, or a selection that pairs users with other fields) the per-user",
              "// form runs, so results always match it. Needs the June 2024 or later engine.",
              "VAR MStart = [Last Full Month Start]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        VAR UserDays =",
              "            ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "                CALCULATETABLE(",
              "                    VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                    REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "                ),",
              "                \"Days\",",
              "                    CALCULATE(",
              "                        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "                        REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "                    )",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 6 && [Days] <= 10)),",
              "        VAR UserDays =",
              "            CALCULATETABLE(",
              "                SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "                    \"Days\", DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "                ),",
              "                REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 6 && [Days] <= 10))",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "2ffa36ba-6aa7-4c3e-b830-fb6b33fef871"
          },
          {
            "name": "Habitual Users, Last Month",
            "description": "Users with 11-15 active days in the last complete calendar month. Slicer-responsive.",
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one SUMMARIZECOLUMNS counts every user's active days, instead of",
              "// one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a",
              "// user slicer, or a selection that pairs users with other fields) the per-user",
              "// form runs, so results always match it. Needs the June 2024 or later engine.",
              "VAR MStart = [Last Full Month Start]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        VAR UserDays =",
              "            ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "                CALCULATETABLE(",
              "                    VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                    REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "                ),",
              "                \"Days\",",
              "                    CALCULATE(",
              "                        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "                        REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "                    )",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 11 && [Days] <= 15)),",
              "        VAR UserDays =",
              "            CALCULATETABLE(",
              "                SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "                    \"Days\", DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "                ),",
              "                REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 11 && [Days] <= 15))",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "8369cb6c-261e-4baf-ad93-5b73c2b9c1cb"
          },
          {
            "name": "Power Users, Last Month",
            "description": [
              "Users with 16+ active days in the last complete calendar month - the habit-formed",
              "cohort. Slicer-responsive. This is the ValueLens equivalent of the AI-in-One",
              "'Licensed Users 16+ Active Days' measure, but WITHOUT the hardcoded licence filter,",
              "so it follows the Environment / Agent Filter slicers instead."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one SUMMARIZECOLUMNS counts every user's active days, instead of",
              "// one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a",
              "// user slicer, or a selection that pairs users with other fields) the per-user",
              "// form runs, so results always match it. Needs the June 2024 or later engine.",
              "VAR MStart = [Last Full Month Start]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        VAR UserDays =",
              "            ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "                CALCULATETABLE(",
              "                    VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                    REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "                ),",
              "                \"Days\",",
              "                    CALCULATE(",
              "                        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "                        REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "                    )",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 16)),",
              "        VAR UserDays =",
              "            CALCULATETABLE(",
              "                SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(",
              "                    'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "                    \"Days\", DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "                ),",
              "                REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 16))",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "3a8bb6a9-ffbc-4a27-95be-37e7c976928b"
          },
          {
            "name": "Stage Base, Last Month",
            "description": [
              "Helper - denominator for the Last Month stage percentages. Inactive plus all active",
              "users in the last complete calendar month, so the five band percentages sum to 100%.",
              "Hidden."
            ],
            "expression": "[Inactive Users, Last Month] + [Active Users, Last Month]",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "isHidden": true,
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "f22db093-5a28-42fd-bce4-34c685d7c875"
          },
          {
            "name": "Inactive Users %, Last Month",
            "description": "Inactive share of the licensed base in the last complete calendar month.",
            "expression": [
              "// Follows [Inactive Users, Last Month]. Without the guard a blank numerator",
              "// would divide to a flat 0%, which reads as \"nobody is inactive\" rather",
              "// than \"this cannot be measured for Cowork\".",
              "VAR _i = [Inactive Users, Last Month]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(NOT ISBLANK(_i), DIVIDE(_i, [Stage Base, Last Month], 0))"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "1058d19b-d3b1-484b-a788-4b617c510796"
          },
          {
            "name": "Beginner Users %, Last Month",
            "description": "Beginner (1-5 active days) share in the last complete calendar month.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Beginner Users, Last Month], [Stage Base, Last Month], 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "bb62f9d3-2725-4782-9a60-eee3dce63e4b"
          },
          {
            "name": "Developing Users %, Last Month",
            "description": "Developing (6-10 active days) share in the last complete calendar month.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Developing Users, Last Month], [Stage Base, Last Month], 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "72e404e7-4e77-4880-a265-8703e47217bf"
          },
          {
            "name": "Habitual Users %, Last Month",
            "description": "Habitual (11-15 active days) share in the last complete calendar month.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Habitual Users, Last Month], [Stage Base, Last Month], 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "65e7b33d-d08e-40bd-8b71-851f91dc9284"
          },
          {
            "name": "Power Users %, Last Month",
            "description": [
              "Power (16+ active days) share in the last complete calendar month - the headline",
              "habit-formation rate. Benchmark from the AI-in-One tenant is roughly 5-8% of",
              "licensed users."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Power Users, Last Month], [Stage Base, Last Month], 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "29bd1b1d-0eda-4d99-93df-4ff3a910c84c"
          },
          {
            "name": "Stage Users, Last Month",
            "description": [
              "Switching measure for the Power Users page. Returns the last-complete-month user",
              "count for whichever band is being evaluated in the 'Stage Legend' disconnected table,",
              "covering the full Inactive -> Power ladder. Drives the stacked monthly chart, the",
              "donut and any stage legend in one field. Fully responsive to the Environment,",
              "Agent Filter, Organization and Date slicers."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR SelectedStage = SELECTEDVALUE('Stage Legend'[Stage])",
              "RETURN",
              "    SWITCH(",
              "        SelectedStage,",
              "        \"0 - Inactive\",   [Inactive Users, Last Month],",
              "        \"1 - Beginner\",   [Beginner Users, Last Month],",
              "        \"2 - Developing\", [Developing Users, Last Month],",
              "        \"3 - Habitual\",   [Habitual Users, Last Month],",
              "        \"4 - Power\",      [Power Users, Last Month],",
              "        BLANK()",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "7e6ce62d-a348-46cf-96c1-bf89b42f0905"
          },
          {
            "name": "Beginner Users (Monthly)",
            "description": [
              "Users with 1-5 active days in the period on the axis.",
              "Evaluated in the CURRENT filter context, so on a month axis each column shows",
              "that month's own count. Fully responsive to Environment / Agent Filter /",
              "Organization slicers."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one SUMMARIZECOLUMNS counts every user's active days, instead of",
              "// one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a",
              "// user slicer, or a selection that pairs users with other fields) the per-user",
              "// form runs, so results always match it. Needs the June 2024 or later engine.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    VAR UserDays =",
              "        ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            \"Days\", CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]))",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 1 && [Days] <= 5)),",
              "    VAR UserDays =",
              "        SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            \"Days\", DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 1 && [Days] <= 5))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Monthly)",
            "lineageTag": "306c254f-7754-4dd0-9e68-83b548e72a45"
          },
          {
            "name": "Developing Users (Monthly)",
            "description": [
              "Users with 6-10 active days in the period on the axis.",
              "Evaluated in the CURRENT filter context, so on a month axis each column shows",
              "that month's own count. Fully responsive to Environment / Agent Filter /",
              "Organization slicers."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one SUMMARIZECOLUMNS counts every user's active days, instead of",
              "// one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a",
              "// user slicer, or a selection that pairs users with other fields) the per-user",
              "// form runs, so results always match it. Needs the June 2024 or later engine.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    VAR UserDays =",
              "        ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            \"Days\", CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]))",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 6 && [Days] <= 10)),",
              "    VAR UserDays =",
              "        SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            \"Days\", DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 6 && [Days] <= 10))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Monthly)",
            "lineageTag": "66e4b56d-e71c-464f-bb17-96ad9282ba3c"
          },
          {
            "name": "Habitual Users (Monthly)",
            "description": [
              "Users with 11-15 active days in the period on the axis.",
              "Evaluated in the CURRENT filter context, so on a month axis each column shows",
              "that month's own count. Fully responsive to Environment / Agent Filter /",
              "Organization slicers."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one SUMMARIZECOLUMNS counts every user's active days, instead of",
              "// one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a",
              "// user slicer, or a selection that pairs users with other fields) the per-user",
              "// form runs, so results always match it. Needs the June 2024 or later engine.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    VAR UserDays =",
              "        ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            \"Days\", CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]))",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 11 && [Days] <= 15)),",
              "    VAR UserDays =",
              "        SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            \"Days\", DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 11 && [Days] <= 15))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Monthly)",
            "lineageTag": "a0a1c196-56a1-47b9-bd72-dd1cd435e3e5"
          },
          {
            "name": "Power Users (Monthly)",
            "description": [
              "Users with 16+ active days in the period on the axis - the habit-formed cohort.",
              "Evaluated in the CURRENT filter context, so on a month axis each column shows",
              "that month's own count. Fully responsive to Environment / Agent Filter /",
              "Organization slicers."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one SUMMARIZECOLUMNS counts every user's active days, instead of",
              "// one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a",
              "// user slicer, or a selection that pairs users with other fields) the per-user",
              "// form runs, so results always match it. Needs the June 2024 or later engine.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    VAR UserDays =",
              "        ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            \"Days\", CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]))",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 16)),",
              "    VAR UserDays =",
              "        SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            \"Days\", DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(UserDays, [Days] >= 16))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Monthly)",
            "lineageTag": "ae9d1da5-461f-483e-8352-7f5826ac9fde"
          },
          {
            "name": "Inactive Users (Monthly)",
            "description": [
              "Licensed users with ZERO activity in the period on the axis. ORG-AWARE via TREATAS so",
              "an organization slicer filters the licensed base as well as the active side.",
              "Blank under an Agents, Cowork or Unlicensed selection, as Inactive Users, Last Month.",
              "",
              "29 Jul 2026 - guarded on Calendar row count. Without the guard the measure returned a",
              "value for the unmatched (blank) date member, because the licensed base comes from",
              "'Copilot Licensed' which has no relationship to Calendar. That produced a phantom",
              "blank column on the monthly stage-mix chart showing the entire licensed population as",
              "Inactive. The guard is axis-agnostic (works on month, week or date axes)."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "// Inactive = holds a Copilot seat but did not use it. Only Copilot has a seat",
              "// list, so the Activity and License slicers (page filters on the audit fact",
              "// table) leave LicensedInScope at the full seat count while the active side",
              "// shrinks to Agents, Cowork or Unlicensed activity - subtracting two different",
              "// populations (measured 11,442 - 183 = 11,316 against 186 observed Cowork",
              "// users). Report nothing rather than a number that cannot be sourced.",
              "VAR Activity = SELECTEDVALUE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)], \"\")",
              "VAR Licence = SELECTEDVALUE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Environment], \"\")",
              "VAR Measured = NOT (Activity IN {\"Agents\", \"Cowork\"}) && Licence <> \"Unlicensed\"",
              "VAR CalRowsInContext = COUNTROWS('Calendar')",
              "VAR LicensedInScope =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        [Total Licensed Users],",
              "        TREATAS(VALUES('Chat + Agent Org Data'[PersonId]), 'Copilot Licensed'[UPN_Normalized])",
              "    )",
              "VAR ActiveLicensed = [Active Licensed Users]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        Measured && CalRowsInContext > 0,",
              "        MAX(LicensedInScope - ActiveLicensed, 0)",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Monthly)",
            "lineageTag": "1362d5d3-0031-4f6a-ba22-294af8787818"
          },
          {
            "name": "Stage Users (Monthly)",
            "description": [
              "Switching measure for the monthly stage-mix chart. Returns the count for",
              "whichever band is being evaluated in the 'Stage Legend' disconnected table,",
              "for the period currently on the axis. Use with:",
              "X axis = 'Calendar'[Year-Month]   Legend = 'Stage Legend'[Stage]",
              "Y      = [Stage Users (Monthly)]"
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR SelectedStage = SELECTEDVALUE('Stage Legend'[Stage])",
              "RETURN",
              "    SWITCH(",
              "        SelectedStage,",
              "        \"0 - Inactive\",   [Inactive Users (Monthly)],",
              "        \"1 - Beginner\",   [Beginner Users (Monthly)],",
              "        \"2 - Developing\", [Developing Users (Monthly)],",
              "        \"3 - Habitual\",   [Habitual Users (Monthly)],",
              "        \"4 - Power\",      [Power Users (Monthly)],",
              "        BLANK()",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Monthly)",
            "lineageTag": "309ca906-d48f-4309-88a2-08bc718f96ff"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork AI Tasks",
            "description": "AI task proxy rows in the Cowork cohort; same base activity definition as AI Tasks.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([AI Tasks], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Value",
            "lineageTag": "95a4b6bf-efb1-46a5-9a1a-d03120f789cb"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Users",
            "description": "Users with Cowork activity: a prompt in Cowork, or a scheduled / autonomous Cowork run.",
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: distinct counts of the IDs with usage rows, less any blank or",
              "// whitespace-only IDs, instead of one CALCULATE per user. When Audit_UserId",
              "// is filtered directly (user rows, a user slicer, or a selection that pairs",
              "// users with other fields) the per-user form runs, so results always match it.",
              "IF(",
              "    ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        COUNTROWS(FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([Usage Rows]) > 0)),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE())",
              "    ),",
              "    VAR BlankIds =",
              "        FILTER(",
              "            ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) = 0",
              "        )",
              "    VAR UsageIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE())",
              "        )",
              "    VAR BlankUsageIds =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()),",
              "            KEEPFILTERS(BlankIds)",
              "        )",
              "    VAR ActiveIds = UsageIds - BlankUsageIds",
              "    RETURN",
              "        IF(ActiveIds > 0, ActiveIds)",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Value",
            "lineageTag": "4b0ffbea-32ff-465c-8989-4b2030f9a1ec"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Sessions",
            "description": "Distinct user, normalized app host and nonblank thread combinations with identifiable user prompts in the selected period. Not timeout-based sessions or verified completed tasks.",
            "expression": [
              "COUNTROWS(",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        SUMMARIZE(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)',",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost_Norm],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]",
              "        ),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Observed Prompt] = TRUE())",
              "    )",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "003f4116-f34f-4b1a-9465-60cbcdade2b1"
          },
          {
            "name": "Session Prompts",
            "description": [
              "Identifiable prompts with a nonempty thread. Numerator for prompts per observed session.",
              "Distinct (user, host, thread, message) prompts on rows flagged Is Observed Prompt - the column",
              "that pre-computes the same row test (prompt row; user, message and thread all present), so the",
              "count is a storage-engine scan instead of a row-by-row FILTER. Replaced CALCULATE([Identifiable",
              "Prompts], thread FILTER) for speed; proven identical across every user, organization, app,",
              "agent, date and thread (ktreadyequiv.py)."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "COUNTROWS(",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        SUMMARIZE(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)',",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost_Norm],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_Id]",
              "        ),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Observed Prompt] = TRUE())",
              "    )",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "cdb3351a-2921-4095-9c34-3efb9c0d34a2"
          },
          {
            "name": "Prompts per Observed Session",
            "description": "Average distinct prompts per observed session, within the current filters. Longer conversations do not necessarily indicate better quality.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Session Prompts], [Observed Sessions])",
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "18dd0439-5e00-4603-b0ee-bd3e130f14d2"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Sessions per User",
            "description": "Observed sessions per active user, using the same prompt-active population as the task proxy.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Observed Sessions], [All Active Users])",
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "7c995f65-ff6e-47c4-b687-b4a317c90508"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Agent Sessions",
            "description": "Observed sessions restricted to the Agent cohort; retains current organization, date and other slicers.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([Observed Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Agents\"))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "b95e4920-ebdd-464b-9e34-29537265095f"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Fit: Surfaces Per Active Day",
            "description": "Measured prompt activity among current active users with no observed Cowork use anywhere in loaded history. Blank apps/dates excluded; Teams aliases merged. A pilot-selection signal, not a suitability score.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _CoworkUsers =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()",
              "    )",
              "VAR _ActiveUsers =",
              "    FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([AI Tasks]) > 0)",
              "VAR _Eligible = EXCEPT(_ActiveUsers, _CoworkUsers)",
              "VAR _Activity =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        FILTER('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)',",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Prompt Row] = TRUE()",
              "                && NOT ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])",
              "                && LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost_Norm])) > 0),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS(TREATAS(_Eligible, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = FALSE())",
              "    )",
              "VAR _Days =",
              "    GROUPBY(",
              "        SUMMARIZE(_Activity, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost_Norm]),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate],",
              "        \"Surfaces\", COUNTX(CURRENTGROUP(), 1)",
              "    )",
              "",
              "RETURN AVERAGEX(_Days, [Surfaces])"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.00",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Fit",
            "lineageTag": "999e830d-8b8a-4106-8bd2-c3c7954429d8"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Licensed Sessions",
            "description": "Observed sessions restricted to the Licensed cohort; retains current organization, date and other slicers.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([Observed Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"M365 Copilot Licensed\"))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "452240cf-e868-43dd-b720-94a12c40629c"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Licensed Sessions per User",
            "description": "Observed Licensed sessions per active cohort user in the selected period.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Observed Licensed Sessions], [Active Licensed Users])",
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "07ef1923-efcd-41e9-8825-07fa6c0293d5"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Licensed Sessions per User per Week",
            "description": "Mean weekly observed Licensed sessions per active cohort user.",
            "expression": [
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"M365 Copilot Licensed\")),",
              "    DIVIDE(CALCULATE([Observed Licensed Sessions]), CALCULATE([Active Licensed Users]))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "b2267480-1975-4e37-aefb-86ac39511665"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Unlicensed Sessions",
            "description": "Observed sessions restricted to the Unlicensed cohort; retains current organization, date and other slicers.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([Observed Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "40b66a9d-3c4e-4d13-b4da-2e49c4613a6b"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Unlicensed Sessions per User",
            "description": "Observed Unlicensed sessions per active cohort user in the selected period.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Observed Unlicensed Sessions], [Active Unlicensed Users])",
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "e38b8f59-37ac-4cc3-8862-fd05803b66be"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Unlicensed Sessions per User per Week",
            "description": "Mean weekly observed Unlicensed sessions per active cohort user.",
            "expression": [
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\")),",
              "    DIVIDE(CALCULATE([Observed Unlicensed Sessions]), CALCULATE([Active Unlicensed Users]))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "66349451-1646-4bc5-9142-57c2ed157236"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Agent Sessions per User",
            "description": "Observed Agent sessions per active cohort user in the selected period.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Observed Agent Sessions], [Active Agent Users])",
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "b1207196-206a-4bc4-a758-e801d12a5373"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Agent Sessions per User per Week",
            "description": "Mean weekly observed Agent sessions per active cohort user.",
            "expression": [
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Agents\")),",
              "    DIVIDE(CALCULATE([Observed Agent Sessions]), CALCULATE([Active Agent Users]))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "ed74cd42-332a-4144-b3e9-7e2770443748"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Cowork Sessions",
            "description": "Observed sessions restricted to the Cowork cohort; retains current organization, date and other slicers.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([Observed Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "5c313a88-6c89-4acd-b1f9-7e637b3ca092"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Cowork Sessions per User",
            "description": "Observed Cowork sessions per active cohort user in the selected period.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Observed Cowork Sessions], [Cowork Users])",
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "a7f5448b-7c32-4d05-b310-ba76cb26ae23"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Cowork Sessions per User per Week",
            "description": "Mean weekly observed Cowork sessions per active cohort user.",
            "expression": [
              "AVERAGEX(",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]), KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE())),",
              "    DIVIDE(CALCULATE([Observed Cowork Sessions]), CALCULATE([Cowork Users]))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "bb5b9974-5362-48c2-b0d1-94572dcfa53c"
          },
          {
            "name": "Observed Sessions per User per Week",
            "description": "Mean weekly observed sessions per active user, consistent with the task-proxy denominator.",
            "expression": [
              "AVERAGEX(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]),",
              "    DIVIDE(CALCULATE([Observed Sessions]), CALCULATE([All Active Users])))"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "1000dfe2-7207-45b9-bdd0-7518367e5bd4"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Top Value Outcome",
            "description": "Cowork-filtered Top Value Outcome: the Cowork Task Category with the most expert equivalent hours, matching the Cowork task breakdown. Hours are modeled estimates, not measured business outcomes.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([Top Value Outcome], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()))",
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Value",
            "lineageTag": "73dba411-55fe-4f61-9c43-f6d3ecf0b284"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Expert Equivalent Hours Per Week",
            "description": "Cowork-filtered Expert Equivalent Hours Per Week; inherited value estimates remain modeled, not measured business outcomes.",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([Expert Equivalent Hours Per Week], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()))",
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Value",
            "lineageTag": "a7162f40-3f91-480e-bcdf-9615af52eb57"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Fit: Eligible Users",
            "description": "Current active users without Cowork activity anywhere in loaded audit history. Existing Cowork users excluded as people, not merely activity rows.",
            "expression": [
              "// Fast path: one distinct count of the IDs with prompt rows, leaving out the Cowork",
              "// users and any blank or whitespace-only IDs, instead of one CALCULATE per user.",
              "// When Audit_UserId is filtered directly (user rows, a user slicer, or a selection",
              "// that pairs users with other fields) the per-user form runs, so results always match it.",
              "VAR _CoworkUsers =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        ISFILTERED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        VAR _ActiveUsers =",
              "            FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([AI Tasks]) > 0)",
              "        VAR _Eligible = EXCEPT(_ActiveUsers, _CoworkUsers)",
              "        RETURN COUNTROWS(_Eligible),",
              "        VAR Excluded =",
              "            UNION(",
              "                _CoworkUsers,",
              "                FILTER(",
              "                    ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                    LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) = 0",
              "                )",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            CALCULATE(",
              "                DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Prompt Row] = TRUE()),",
              "                KEEPFILTERS(EXCEPT(ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]), Excluded))",
              "            )",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Fit",
            "lineageTag": "dcc6dc3a-29e4-4f86-b660-843543357fb9"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Fit: Session Depth",
            "description": "Prompts per observed session for the non-Cowork active cohort; no readiness threshold.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _CoworkUsers =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()",
              "    )",
              "VAR _ActiveUsers =",
              "    FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([AI Tasks]) > 0)",
              "VAR _Eligible = EXCEPT(_ActiveUsers, _CoworkUsers)",
              "RETURN CALCULATE([Prompts per Observed Session], KEEPFILTERS(TREATAS(_Eligible, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])))",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0.00",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Fit",
            "lineageTag": "52cdb33d-28af-468b-877e-ae1590f02b5f"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Fit: Agent User Share",
            "description": "Share of eligible active users with observed agent activity in the selected context.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _CoworkUsers =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()",
              "    )",
              "VAR _ActiveUsers =",
              "    FILTER(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])) > 0 && CALCULATE([AI Tasks]) > 0)",
              "VAR _Eligible = EXCEPT(_ActiveUsers, _CoworkUsers)",
              "RETURN DIVIDE(",
              "    CALCULATE([Active Agent Users], KEEPFILTERS(TREATAS(_Eligible, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]))),",
              "    COUNTROWS(_Eligible))",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Fit",
            "lineageTag": "39bd0a67-fe7c-42e0-9fec-450899279da7"
          },
          {
            "name": "Median Unlicensed Sessions Per User Per Week",
            "description": [
              "Session-grain counterpart of 'Median Unlicensed AI Tasks Per User Per Week'.",
              "Typical (median) unlicensed user's weekly session count, so a few very heavy",
              "users cannot inflate the figure the way a mean would. Built on",
              "[Observed Unlicensed Sessions] so it inherits the session grain",
              "(user + AppHost + thread) and the evidence guards on prompt rows."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "MEDIANX(",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        CALCULATE([Observed Unlicensed Sessions]) > 0",
              "    ),",
              "    VAR TotalSessions =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            [Observed Unlicensed Sessions],",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    VAR TotalWeeks =",
              "        CALCULATE(",
              "            DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart]),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\",",
              "            REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[WeekStart])",
              "        )",
              "    RETURN",
              "        DIVIDE(TotalSessions, TotalWeeks, 0)",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Sessions & Tasks",
            "lineageTag": "3f7c1a92-5d48-4e63-9b21-0c7ad4e15b88"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Readiness: Surfaces Per Day",
            "description": [
              "Average number of distinct apps (normalized hosts) a user prompted in per active day,",
              "excluding Cowork. Written as user-day-app combinations / user-day combinations, which equals",
              "the average of each user-day's app count, without materializing the fact table row by row.",
              "Proven identical to the previous AVERAGEX over a GROUPBY (ktreadyequiv.py)."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _UserDayApp =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        SUMMARIZE(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)',",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost_Norm]",
              "        ),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Prompt Row] = TRUE()),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = FALSE()),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS(NOT ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate])),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS(",
              "            FILTER(",
              "                VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost_Norm]),",
              "                LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost_Norm])) > 0",
              "            )",
              "        )",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    DIVIDE(",
              "        COUNTROWS(_UserDayApp),",
              "        COUNTROWS(",
              "            SUMMARIZE(",
              "                _UserDayApp,",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]",
              "            )",
              "        )",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.00",
            "displayFolder": "Cowork Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "52ebeeba-b5d3-41a5-8999-69ecb2a42224"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Readiness Rank (Dynamic)",
            "description": [
              "Dense rank of the Cowork score, recalculated against the current selection.",
              "Ranks users when Audit_UserId is in scope (within their organization when",
              "Organization is also in scope), otherwise organizations. The",
              "candidate table is built context-free so the engine caches it across rows",
              "(this is what keeps a 138-candidate table under a second)."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _Scope =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        FILTER(",
              "            ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "                ALLSELECTED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                \"@b\", [Cowork Readiness: Surfaces Per Day],",
              "                \"@d\", CALCULATE([Prompts per Observed Session], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = FALSE())),",
              "                \"@a\", IF(COALESCE(CALCULATE([Observed Agent Sessions]), 0) > 0, 1, 0),",
              "                \"@cw\", COALESCE(CALCULATE([Observed Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE())), 0)",
              "            ),",
              "            [@cw] = 0 && NOT ISBLANK([@b]) && NOT ISBLANK([@d])",
              "        ),",
              "        ALLSELECTED()",
              "    )",
              "VAR _MaxB = MAXX(_Scope, [@b])",
              "VAR _MaxD = MAXX(_Scope, [@d])",
              "VAR _AllScored = ADDCOLUMNS(_Scope, \"@s\", ROUND(",
              "                45 * MIN(DIVIDE([@b], _MaxB, 0), 1)",
              "              + 35 * MIN(DIVIDE([@d], _MaxD, 0), 1)",
              "              + 20 * [@a],",
              "                0",
              "            ))",
              "VAR _LocalMe =",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "                \"@b\", [Cowork Readiness: Surfaces Per Day],",
              "                \"@d\", CALCULATE([Prompts per Observed Session], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = FALSE())),",
              "                \"@a\", IF(COALESCE(CALCULATE([Observed Agent Sessions]), 0) > 0, 1, 0),",
              "                \"@cw\", COALESCE(CALCULATE([Observed Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE())), 0)",
              "        ),",
              "        [@cw] = 0 && NOT ISBLANK([@b]) && NOT ISBLANK([@d])",
              "    )",
              "VAR _ScoredMe = ADDCOLUMNS(_LocalMe, \"@s\", ROUND(",
              "                45 * MIN(DIVIDE([@b], _MaxB, 0), 1)",
              "              + 35 * MIN(DIVIDE([@d], _MaxD, 0), 1)",
              "              + 20 * [@a],",
              "                0",
              "            ))",
              "VAR _Me = IF(COUNTROWS(_ScoredMe) = 0, BLANK(), ROUND(AVERAGEX(_ScoredMe, [@s]), 0))",
              "VAR _IsUserLevel = ISINSCOPE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId])",
              "-- Organization level: every user belongs to one organization (many-to-one on PersonId),",
              "-- so an organization's score is the rounded average of its users' scores, which",
              "-- _AllScored already holds for the whole selection. Joining each user to their",
              "-- organization once replaces rebuilding the user table for every organization.",
              "-- Scores are whole numbers, so SUM / COUNT equals the previous AVERAGEX exactly.",
              "-- Proven identical at user and organization level (ktrankequiv2.py).",
              "VAR _UserOrg =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        SUMMARIZE(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)',",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization]",
              "        ),",
              "        ALLSELECTED()",
              "    )",
              "-- Users nested under an organization rank within that organization, as on the",
              "-- License Readiness table; without an organization in scope they rank across the selection.",
              "VAR _OrgScoped = ISINSCOPE('Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization])",
              "VAR _CurOrg = SELECTEDVALUE('Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization])",
              "VAR _ByOrg =",
              "    ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "        GROUPBY(",
              "            NATURALINNERJOIN(_AllScored, _UserOrg),",
              "            'Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization],",
              "            \"@sum\", SUMX(CURRENTGROUP(), [@s]),",
              "            \"@n\", COUNTX(CURRENTGROUP(), [@s])",
              "        ),",
              "        \"@os\", IF([@n] = 0, BLANK(), ROUND(DIVIDE([@sum], [@n]), 0))",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        ISBLANK(_Me),",
              "        BLANK(),",
              "        IF(",
              "            _IsUserLevel,",
              "            IF(",
              "                _OrgScoped,",
              "                COUNTROWS(",
              "                    FILTER(",
              "                        DISTINCT(",
              "                            SELECTCOLUMNS(",
              "                                FILTER(NATURALINNERJOIN(_AllScored, _UserOrg), 'Chat + Agent Org Data'[Organization] = _CurOrg),",
              "                                \"@v\", [@s]",
              "                            )",
              "                        ),",
              "                        [@v] > _Me",
              "                    )",
              "                ) + 1,",
              "                COUNTROWS(FILTER(DISTINCT(SELECTCOLUMNS(_AllScored, \"@v\", [@s])), [@v] > _Me)) + 1",
              "            ),",
              "            COUNTROWS(",
              "                FILTER(",
              "                    DISTINCT(SELECTCOLUMNS(FILTER(_ByOrg, NOT ISBLANK([@os])), \"@v\", [@os])),",
              "                    [@v] > _Me",
              "                )",
              "            ) + 1",
              "        )",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Cowork Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "a615880c-4403-45f9-9aab-f45891a0a0a6"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Readiness: Prompts Per Session",
            "expression": "CALCULATE([Prompts per Observed Session], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = FALSE()))",
            "formatString": "0.00",
            "displayFolder": "Cowork Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "658abd37-a14f-4c29-8275-eee823b20f2a"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Consumption Tasks",
            "description": "Tasks billed through the consumption surface (Cowork) in the current selection.",
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    [AI Prompts],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\")",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0003-0003-0001-0001-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "User Active Days, Last Month",
            "expression": [
              "VAR MStart = [Last Full Month Start]",
              "RETURN",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Calendar'),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[MonthStart] = MStart",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "ff0e0001-0001-0001-0001-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "User Stage, Last Month",
            "description": [
              "Maturity stage for the CURRENT selection, derived from",
              "[User Active Days, Last Month] using the published 5-stage band edges.",
              "A user with no activity in the last complete month returns \"0 - Inactive\";",
              "no stage is ever guessed from a different month."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _D = COALESCE([User Active Days, Last Month], 0)",
              "RETURN",
              "    SWITCH(",
              "        TRUE(),",
              "        _D = 0,   \"0 - Inactive\",",
              "        _D <= 5,  \"1 - Beginner\",",
              "        _D <= 10, \"2 - Developing\",",
              "        _D <= 15, \"3 - Habitual\",",
              "        \"4 - Power\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "ff0e0001-0001-0001-0001-000000000002"
          },
          {
            "name": "Maturity Row Filter",
            "description": [
              "Row gate for the User Maturity List table. Returns 1 when the person belongs",
              "in the maturity base (licensed, OR active in the last complete month) AND",
              "matches the Stage slicer. Used as a visual-level filter so the table lists",
              "genuinely inactive licensed users, not only people who show up in the logs."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _Licensed =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        [Total Licensed Users],",
              "        TREATAS(VALUES('Chat + Agent Org Data'[PersonId]), 'Copilot Licensed'[UPN_Normalized])",
              "    )",
              "VAR _Days = COALESCE([User Active Days, Last Month], 0)",
              "VAR _InBase = COALESCE(_Licensed, 0) > 0 || _Days > 0",
              "VAR _Stage = [User Stage, Last Month]",
              "VAR _NoStageSel = NOT ISFILTERED('Stage Legend'[Stage])",
              "VAR _StageOk =",
              "    IF(_NoStageSel, TRUE(), _Stage IN VALUES('Stage Legend'[Stage]))",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(_InBase && _StageOk, 1, 0)"
            ],
            "formatString": "0",
            "isHidden": true,
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "ff0e0001-0001-0001-0001-000000000004"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Alternative Tool",
            "description": [
              "Names the cheaper surface for work the page has already judged a simple ask, and",
              "carries the evidence for it: how much comparable work in-app Copilot Chat already",
              "handles. Blank on Strong and Fair fit rows, and blank when no comparable Copilot",
              "volume exists, so the table never invents an alternative.",
              "",
              "WHAT COMPARABLE MEANS. Every one of the 26 Behavior_Category values in the feed",
              "joins to 'Human Time Estimates'[Behavior], which tags each behaviour with a Cowork",
              "Category. So for a given task category the matching Copilot behaviours are known,",
              "and the comparator counts real Copilot prompts in exactly those behaviours.",
              "",
              "TWO FAULTS THIS REPLACES. The previous version gated on",
              "Session Turn Band = \"1 turn\", which matches only 337 of 39,222 Cowork tasks - that",
              "column counts audit ROWS per thread, so an attachment-heavy prompt reads as many",
              "turns and 36,390 tasks land in \"7+ turns\". It then let the Copilot comparator",
              "inherit the Cowork Task Category row filter, and that column is blank outside",
              "Cowork, so the comparator filtered itself to nothing. Between them the column was",
              "empty on every row."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _low = [Usage Efficiency: Low Fit Tasks]",
              "VAR _cat = SELECTEDVALUE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category])",
              "// IF cannot return a table in DAX, so the blank-category case is folded",
              "// into the row filter instead of branching.",
              "VAR _behaviours =",
              "    SELECTCOLUMNS(",
              "        FILTER(",
              "            ALL('Human Time Estimates'),",
              "            ISBLANK(_cat)",
              "                || 'Human Time Estimates'[Cowork Category] = _cat",
              "        ),",
              "        \"@behaviour\", 'Human Time Estimates'[Behavior]",
              "    )",
              "VAR _alt =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        [AI Prompts],",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS(",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AppHost_Norm],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Turn Band],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade],",
              "            'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Behavior_Category]",
              "        ),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Copilot\"),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Behavior_Category] IN _behaviours)",
              "    )",
              "VAR _txt =",
              "    SWITCH(",
              "        TRUE(),",
              "        _alt >= 1000000, FORMAT(DIVIDE(_alt, 1000000), \"0.0\") & \"M\",",
              "        _alt >= 1000, FORMAT(DIVIDE(_alt, 1000), \"0\") & \"K\",",
              "        FORMAT(_alt, \"#,##0\")",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        COALESCE(_low, 0) = 0 || COALESCE(_alt, 0) = 0,",
              "        BLANK(),",
              "        \"Copilot Chat (\" & _txt & \" similar)\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff0e0002-0002-0001-0001-000000000002"
          },
          {
            "name": "AI Prompts",
            "description": [
              "Distinct prompts (turns) in the current selection - one per Message_Id. [AI Tasks]",
              "counts audit ROWS instead, and a prompt emits one row per resource reference, so it",
              "runs 2.6x higher than the prompt count model-wide and 5.4x inside Cowork. Every",
              "figure that describes what a prompt did must use this, not [AI Tasks]."
            ],
            "expression": "DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_Id])",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Value Types",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0004-0001-0001-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Attributed Tasks",
            "description": "Tasks in the current selection that carry a model name at all.",
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    [AI Prompts],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Model Cost Tier] <> \"Not attributed\")",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0002-0001-0001-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Attribution Coverage",
            "description": "Share of tasks carrying a model name. Every other model figure describes this share only.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Model: Attributed Tasks], [AI Prompts])",
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0002-0001-0001-000000000002"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Coverage Notice",
            "description": [
              "The one \"how to read\" box on Model Fit: the three match outcomes in plain words (with the Verdict",
              "icon glyphs), the Verdict rule, that the fit grade is the Cowork Fit rule applied to every tool at the",
              "grading setting chosen in Assumptions, and the model-logged base (sessions and prompts) - so no tier",
              "figure is read as more than a heuristic."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _s = [Model: Sessions]",
              "VAR _ls = [Model: Logged Session Share]",
              "VAR _lp = [Model: Attribution Coverage]",
              "VAR _mode = [Fit Grading Value]",
              "RETURN",
              "    SWITCH(",
              "        TRUE(),",
              "        COALESCE(_s, 0) = 0, \"No activity in this selection.\",",
              "        COALESCE(_ls, 0) = 0, \"No session here carries a model name, so model fit cannot be judged.\",",
              "        \"✓ GOOD MATCH · the model tier suits the work     ↓ LIGHTER MODEL MAY DO · a Frontier model on work graded Worth a look     ↑ TRY STRONGER · a mid-tier model on Strong-fit work, where Cowork or a Frontier model may do better.   VERDICT = the most common of the three (grey = under 5 judged). Same fit grade as Cowork Fit (\"",
              "            & _mode & \" grading, set in Assumptions); a session is judged only when its model is logged and it has a grade. Model logged on \"",
              "            & FORMAT(_ls, \"0.0%\") & \" of sessions (\" & FORMAT(_lp, \"0.0%\") & \" of prompts). A prompt to test, not a quality score.\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0002-0001-0001-000000000003"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks",
            "description": "Cowork sessions that carry enough evidence to be graded at all.",
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    [Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] <> \"Unclassified\")",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0003-0001-0001-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Fit Rule Notice",
            "description": [
              "The one \"how to read\" box on Cowork Fit: the three grades in plain words for the grading setting in",
              "Assumptions, what the grade can and cannot see (so a flag reads as a coaching prompt, not a verdict on",
              "Cowork's value), the graded base and how many sessions carry too little detail to grade."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _g = [Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks]",
              "VAR _u =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        [Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions],",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Unclassified\")",
              "    )",
              "VAR _mode = [Fit Grading Value]",
              "VAR _fair =",
              "    SWITCH(",
              "        _mode,",
              "        \"Strict\", \"some sources\",",
              "        \"Lenient\", \"some sources, messages read, one app or a longer chat\",",
              "        \"some sources, messages read or one app\"",
              "    )",
              "VAR _worth =",
              "    SWITCH(",
              "        _mode,",
              "        \"Strict\", \"chat only or one app\",",
              "        \"Lenient\", \"a one-turn chat with nothing read or attached\",",
              "        \"chat with nothing read or attached\"",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        COALESCE(_g, 0) = 0,",
              "        \"Nothing in this selection carries enough detail to assess.\",",
              "        \"STRONG · spans apps, builds a file or uses many sources     FAIR · \" & _fair",
              "            & \"     WORTH A LOOK · \" & _worth",
              "            & \".   We see what a session touched, not prompts or answer quality: a flag is a coaching prompt, not a verdict. \"",
              "            & FORMAT(_g, \"#,##0\") & \" graded\"",
              "            & IF(COALESCE(_u, 0) = 0, \"\", \"; \" & FORMAT(_u, \"#,##0\") & \" too light to grade\")",
              "            & \". Grading: \" & _mode & \" (Assumptions).\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0003-0001-0001-000000000003"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Low Fit Tasks",
            "description": [
              "Consumption SESSIONS graded Worth a look - nothing shows the session needed Cowork (at Balanced",
              "grading, chat where nothing was read or attached). Keeps its original name because visuals bind to it."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    [Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Worth a look\")",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc000001-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Hours (Task Category Basis)",
            "description": [
              "Cowork-only expert-equivalent hours: how long a skilled professional would take to do",
              "by hand the work Cowork sessions did. Computed exactly as What-I-did-with-Cowork does.",
              "",
              "METHOD (WIDWC compute.py:138-144). For every session x task category it touched:",
              "runs x the category's published CATS band, in minutes. Bands, Low / Typical / High:",
              "Analysis 30/67/92, Document 12/24/42, Email 3/7/12, Meeting 12/31/43, Comms 2/4/11,",
              "Specialized 10/25/40, Code 30/56/96, General 2/5/8. The Effort Scenario slicer picks the",
              "column; the Adj sliders still scale each category.",
              "",
              "RUNS (WIDWC mine_session.py:171-179). Document, Specialized and General work count once",
              "per session. Tool-heavy categories count one run per chain of tool calls:",
              "max(1, round(calls / chain)), chain = Analysis 5, Email 4, Comms 4, Meeting 3, Code 6.",
              "Audit logs have no tool-call log, so calls = resource reads (rows with a typed",
              "AccessedResource_Type other than \"message\"). round() is banker's rounding, as in Python.",
              "",
              "WHY THIS REPLACED THE PER-PROMPT BASIS. The earlier version charged a behaviour-averaged",
              "rate per prompt and rejected the CATS bands because per turn they over-count (2,363 h) and",
              "once per session they under-count (772 h). WIDWC's own runs rule is the middle path that",
              "analysis did not test: long read-heavy analysis earns more runs, a one-line ask earns one.",
              "On this data: 2,746 h Typical (1,241 Conservative, 3,956 Optimistic), against 488 h",
              "hands-on - a 5.6x speed multiplier. The WIDWC demo shows 6.8x for one power user; this",
              "estate is dominated by short General-assistance sessions at a 5-minute band."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _scn = [Effort Scenario Selected]",
              "RETURN",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        SUMX(",
              "            SUMMARIZE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)', 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category]),",
              "            VAR _c = 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category]",
              "            VAR _lo =",
              "                SWITCH(_c,",
              "                    \"Analysis & Research\", 30, \"Document & content creation\", 12,",
              "                    \"Email workflows\", 3, \"Meeting workflows\", 12,",
              "                    \"Communication workflows\", 2, \"Specialized workflows\", 10,",
              "                    \"Write or debug code\", 30, \"General assistance / Other\", 2, BLANK())",
              "            VAR _typ =",
              "                SWITCH(_c,",
              "                    \"Analysis & Research\", 67, \"Document & content creation\", 24,",
              "                    \"Email workflows\", 7, \"Meeting workflows\", 31,",
              "                    \"Communication workflows\", 4, \"Specialized workflows\", 25,",
              "                    \"Write or debug code\", 56, \"General assistance / Other\", 5, BLANK())",
              "            VAR _hi =",
              "                SWITCH(_c,",
              "                    \"Analysis & Research\", 92, \"Document & content creation\", 42,",
              "                    \"Email workflows\", 12, \"Meeting workflows\", 43,",
              "                    \"Communication workflows\", 11, \"Specialized workflows\", 40,",
              "                    \"Write or debug code\", 96, \"General assistance / Other\", 8, BLANK())",
              "            VAR _band = SWITCH(_scn, \"Conservative\", _lo, \"Optimistic\", _hi, _typ)",
              "            VAR _chain =",
              "                SWITCH(_c,",
              "                    \"Analysis & Research\", 5, \"Email workflows\", 4,",
              "                    \"Communication workflows\", 4, \"Meeting workflows\", 3,",
              "                    \"Write or debug code\", 6, 0)",
              "            VAR _reads =",
              "                IF(",
              "                    _chain > 0,",
              "                    CALCULATE(",
              "                        COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "                        KEEPFILTERS(",
              "                            FILTER(",
              "                                VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AccessedResource_Type]),",
              "                                NOT ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AccessedResource_Type])",
              "                                    && LEN(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AccessedResource_Type])) > 0",
              "                                    && LOWER(TRIM('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AccessedResource_Type])) <> \"message\"",
              "                            )",
              "                        )",
              "                    )",
              "                )",
              "            VAR _q = DIVIDE(_reads, _chain, 0)",
              "            VAR _whole = INT(_q)",
              "            VAR _frac = _q - _whole",
              "            VAR _rounded = IF(_frac > 0.5 || (_frac = 0.5 && ISODD(_whole)), _whole + 1, _whole)",
              "            VAR _runs = IF(_chain > 0, MAX(1, _rounded), 1)",
              "            VAR _mult =",
              "                SWITCH(_c,",
              "                    \"Email workflows\", [Adj Comms],",
              "                    \"Communication workflows\", [Adj Comms],",
              "                    \"Meeting workflows\", [Adj Meetings],",
              "                    \"Document & content creation\", [Adj Content],",
              "                    \"Write or debug code\", [Adj Content],",
              "                    \"Analysis & Research\", [Adj Search],",
              "                    [Adj Agents])",
              "            RETURN",
              "                IF(ISBLANK(_band), 0, DIVIDE(_runs * _band * _mult, 60, 0))",
              "        ),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\")",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Time Savings",
            "lineageTag": "fc000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000004"
          },
          {
            "name": "Human Equivalent Hours (Behaviour Basis)",
            "description": [
              "Total human-equivalent hours: what AI is handling that humans would otherwise do.",
              "Basis: Cowork Methodology v4 minutes-per-turn bands (Low / Typical / High), selected",
              "via the Effort Scenario slicer. Uncertainty is carried by the band, not a hidden haircut.",
              "",
              "GRAIN. The audit table is exploded to one row per message x accessed resource",
              "(measured 2.65 rows per prompt). Effort is therefore accrued two different ways:",
              "Per Resource - retrieval and consumption behaviours whose extra rows were measured",
              "to be ~100% distinct resources with ~0% empty references. Each",
              "resource is a document a person would genuinely have had to open,",
              "so every row accrues effort.",
              "Per Turn     - everything else. Counted once per prompt, because the Cowork band",
              "already embeds multi-instance chaining (e.g. 6.1 min x 4 instances);",
              "accruing per row would apply that assumption twice.",
              "Per-category customer sliders (Adj: Comms/Meetings/Content/Search/Agents) still apply."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    VAR _scn = [Effort Scenario Selected]",
              "    RETURN",
              "    SUMX(",
              "        VALUES('Behavior Value Map'[Behavior]),",
              "        VAR _cat   = CALCULATE(MAX('Human Time Estimates'[Category]))",
              "        VAR _grain = CALCULATE(MAX('Human Time Estimates'[Effort Grain]))",
              "        VAR _min =",
              "            SWITCH(",
              "                _scn,",
              "                \"Conservative\", CALCULATE(MAX('Human Time Estimates'[Min Low])),",
              "                \"Optimistic\", CALCULATE(MAX('Human Time Estimates'[Min High])),",
              "                CALCULATE(MAX('Human Time Estimates'[Min Typical]))",
              "            )",
              "        VAR _mult =",
              "            SWITCH(",
              "                _cat,",
              "                \"Email\", [Adj Comms],",
              "                \"Collaboration & Workflows\", [Adj Comms],",
              "                \"Meetings\", [Adj Meetings],",
              "                \"Document Creation\", [Adj Content],",
              "                \"Document Summarisation\", [Adj Content],",
              "                \"Presentations\", [Adj Content],",
              "                \"Creative & Design\", [Adj Content],",
              "                \"Coding & Technical\", [Adj Content],",
              "                \"Search & Research\", [Adj Search],",
              "                \"Data & Analysis\", [Adj Search],",
              "                \"Specialist Support\", [Adj Agents],",
              "                \"General Chat & Q&A\", [Adj Agents],",
              "                1",
              "            )",
              "        VAR _b = 'Behavior Value Map'[Behavior]",
              "        VAR _msgs =",
              "            CALCULATE(",
              "                DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_Id]),",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "            )",
              "        VAR _rows =",
              "            CALCULATE(",
              "                COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "            )",
              "        // this behaviour's mean resources per prompt, measured across the whole",
              "        // window so a filtered view is weighted against the org norm, not itself",
              "        VAR _meanRes =",
              "            CALCULATE(",
              "                DIVIDE(",
              "                    COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "                    DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_Id])",
              "                ),",
              "                REMOVEFILTERS(),",
              "                'Behavior Value Map'[Behavior] = _b,",
              "                'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Message_isPrompt] = \"TRUE\"",
              "            )",
              "        VAR _units =",
              "            IF(",
              "                _grain = \"Per Resource\" && _meanRes > 0,",
              "                DIVIDE(_rows, _meanRes),",
              "                _msgs",
              "            )",
              "        RETURN",
              "            DIVIDE(_min * _mult * _units, 60, 0)",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Time Savings",
            "lineageTag": "ff060001-0001-0001-0001-000000000010"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions",
            "description": [
              "Cowork sessions (threads). The fit page's counting unit: fit is graded per",
              "session, so it is counted per session. Counting prompts instead would weight",
              "each session by how chatty it was and over-credit long ones."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]),",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\")",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000003"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Evidence Files",
            "description": [
              "SOURCE ITEMS. Median pieces of source material a Cowork session worked across - attached",
              "files, links and pasted text, NOT only file attachments. The depth half of Work Weight",
              "Grade. Counted from AccessedResource_Type, a MIME type; blanks and \"message\" are excluded,",
              "so a plain conversational turn contributes nothing. A file re-listed on a later prompt",
              "counts again, as it does in the fit rule.",
              "MEDIAN, not mean. Reference counts are heavy-tailed: one email session read 1,835 items in",
              "a single prompt, which dragged the Email mean to 111.8 while its typical session used 7.",
              "Counted exactly as the fit rule counts them (Session Material Refs), so the figure shown",
              "is the same evidence that decided the grade."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _s =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\"",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        NOT ISEMPTY(_s),",
              "        MEDIANX(_s, CALCULATE(MAX('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Material Refs])))",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0003-0001-0001-000000000031"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Evidence Kinds",
            "description": [
              "SOURCE TYPES. Median number of DISTINCT source types a Cowork session worked across - the",
              "breadth half of the grade. Same filter as Source items, but distinct MIME types rather",
              "than occurrences: ten spreadsheets are 10 items and 1 type. Median for the same reason."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _s =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId]),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\"",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        NOT ISEMPTY(_s),",
              "        MEDIANX(_s, CALCULATE(MAX('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Material Types])))",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0003-0001-0001-000000000032"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cohort Is Cowork",
            "description": [
              "1 when the current selection is scoped to Cowork alone, otherwise 0.",
              "The cohort buttons are page filters on [Agent Filter (Normalized)], so a",
              "single visible value of \"Cowork\" is the signal. Used by measures that",
              "cannot be sourced for Cowork because Cowork carries no seat inventory."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "INT(",
              "    SELECTEDVALUE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)], \"\") = \"Cowork\"",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0",
            "isHidden": true,
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Habit Formation (Last Month)",
            "lineageTag": "fc000011-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Fit Basis",
            "description": [
              "The test that decided the grade for most sessions in this row, with the share",
              "it covers. Counted from [Fit Basis]; nothing is inferred. Answers \"why is the",
              "same kind of work strong fit here and worth a look there\" - the answer is always the",
              "material the session carried."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _bases =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Fit Basis]),",
              "        'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\"",
              "    )",
              "VAR _t = ADDCOLUMNS(_bases, \"@n\", [Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions])",
              "VAR _n = SUMX(_t, [@n])",
              "VAR _top = TOPN(1, _t, [@n], DESC)",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        COALESCE(_n, 0) > 0,",
              "        MAXX(_top, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Fit Basis])",
              "            & \" (\" & FORMAT(DIVIDE(MAXX(_top, [@n]), _n), \"0%\") & \")\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc000011-0000-0000-0000-000000000003"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Active Days Per User",
            "description": [
              "Mean distinct days a Cowork user was active, in the current selection.",
              "",
              "The reference report is personal, so its ACTIVE DAYS card is one user's day count. At",
              "estate grain a raw distinct-day count would just report the length of the window, so",
              "this is per user, which is the comparable figure."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _users = [Cowork Users]",
              "VAR _userDays =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        SUMX(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "            CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]))",
              "        ),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\")",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(COALESCE(_users, 0) > 0, DIVIDE(_userDays, _users))"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0.0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000b1-0000-0000-0000-000000000003"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Logged Session Share",
            "description": [
              "Share of sessions (every tool) with a model name logged on at least one row - the base every tier",
              "figure on this page stands on. The remainder is Not attributed and cannot be judged."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "DIVIDE(",
              "    CALCULATE([Model: Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Model Tier] <> \"Not attributed\")),",
              "    [Model: Sessions]",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000c1-0000-0000-0000-000000000011"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Over-specified Share",
            "description": [
              "LIGHTER MODEL MAY DO share (HEURISTIC SIGNAL, not a verdict): premium model on work graded Worth a look,",
              "as a share of judged sessions. With Good match and Try stronger it adds to 100%."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Model: Over-specified Sessions], [Model: Judged Sessions])",
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000c1-0000-0000-0000-000000000013"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Well-matched Share",
            "description": "GOOD MATCH share: judged sessions whose model cost tier suited the fit grade of the work.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Model: Well-matched Sessions], [Model: Judged Sessions])",
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000c1-0000-0000-0000-000000000014"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Share Of Work",
            "description": [
              "The \"% of work\" column on the Cowork Fit WHY table (Grade -> how it was done): each row's share of",
              "the graded Cowork work in the selection. Grade rows add to 100% and work-shape rows add to their grade.",
              "The grade is taken out of the base, so clicking a Strong / Fair / Worth a look segment on the WHAT chart keeps",
              "the base at the whole task: the Strong row then reads \"share of this task that was Strong fit\".",
              "Unit: with Cowork Task Category on rows the unit is a session x category pair, because one session",
              "can span several categories (so there are more pairs than graded sessions); otherwise",
              "it is graded sessions."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _byCat = ISINSCOPE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category])",
              "VAR _num =",
              "    IF(",
              "        _byCat,",
              "        SUMX(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category]), [Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks]),",
              "        [Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks]",
              "    )",
              "VAR _den =",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        IF(",
              "            _byCat,",
              "            SUMX(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category]), [Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks]),",
              "            [Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks]",
              "        ),",
              "        ALLSELECTED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Cowork Task Category]),",
              "        ALLSELECTED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Shape], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Shape Sort]),",
              "        ALLSELECTED('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Model Tier], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Model Tier Sort]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort])",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    DIVIDE(_num, _den)"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "ff0d0009-0003-0001-0001-000000000010"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Sessions",
            "description": [
              "Sessions (threads) across every tool - Copilot, agents and Cowork - the Model Fit page's counting",
              "unit, because fit and model tier are both decided per thread. Blank thread IDs (765 Copilot rows)",
              "are not a session and are excluded. Differs from Observed Sessions, which splits a thread by user",
              "and app host and needs an identifiable prompt."
            ],
            "expression": "DISTINCTCOUNTNOBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[ThreadId])",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000002"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Judged Sessions",
            "description": [
              "Sessions where model fit can be judged: a graded session with a known tier (Frontier or Workhorse).",
              "The base every match share on the page divides by, so Good match + Lighter model may do + Try stronger = 100%."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    [Model: Sessions],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Model Tier] IN {\"Frontier (premium cost)\", \"Workhorse (mid cost)\"}),",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] IN {\"Strong fit\", \"Fair fit\", \"Worth a look\"})",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000004"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Over-specified Sessions",
            "description": [
              "LIGHTER MODEL MAY DO on the Model Fit page (plain label for \"over-specified\").",
              "HEURISTIC SIGNAL: sessions on a Frontier (premium cost) model whose work graded Worth a look - at",
              "Balanced grading, chat where nothing was read or attached. Worth testing on a lighter model; nothing",
              "in the audit log shows a lighter model would have answered as well."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    [Model: Sessions],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Model Tier] = \"Frontier (premium cost)\"),",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Worth a look\")",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000005"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Under-specified Sessions",
            "description": [
              "TRY STRONGER on the Model Fit page (plain label for \"under-specified\"). HEURISTIC SIGNAL: sessions on a",
              "Workhorse (mid cost) model whose work graded Strong fit - spanned 2+ apps, built an artifact, or used many",
              "sources. Candidates to try on a Frontier model or in Cowork, not failures: GPT-5 (Next Gen) logs no",
              "reasoning mode, and nothing here measures answer quality."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    [Model: Sessions],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Session Model Tier] = \"Workhorse (mid cost)\"),",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Strong fit\")",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000006"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Well-matched Sessions",
            "description": [
              "GOOD MATCH on the Model Fit page. Judged sessions that are neither Lighter model may do nor Try stronger: Frontier",
              "on Strong or Fair fit work, Workhorse on Fair fit or Worth a look. Tier and grade are both one value per session,",
              "so the three buckets partition Judged Sessions exactly."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _j = [Model: Judged Sessions]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        COALESCE(_j, 0) > 0,",
              "        _j - COALESCE([Model: Over-specified Sessions], 0) - COALESCE([Model: Under-specified Sessions], 0)",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000007"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Not Judged Sessions",
            "description": [
              "NOT JUDGED: sessions model fit cannot speak to - no model name logged anywhere in the session, or too",
              "little evidence to grade the work. Shown, not hidden, so the judged share is always read against it."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _n = [Model: Sessions] - COALESCE([Model: Judged Sessions], 0)",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(_n > 0, _n)"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000008"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Under-specified Share",
            "description": [
              "TRY STRONGER share (HEURISTIC SIGNAL): mid-cost model on Strong-fit work, as a share of judged sessions -",
              "worth testing on Frontier or in Cowork."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Model: Under-specified Sessions], [Model: Judged Sessions])",
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000009"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Fit Icon",
            "description": [
              "FIT ICON for the fit tables - read at a glance, like the What-I-did-with-Cowork report's grade dot.",
              "One grade in the row (every \"How it was done\" row, which IS one rule step): a coloured circle with its",
              "mark - S (Strong fit) teal, F (Fair fit) coral, ? (Worth a look) crimson, the same colours as the fit",
              "charts. Several grades (a task-category row or the total): a bar split in proportion to Strong / Fair /",
              "Worth a look sessions, so a parent row shows its mix instead of pretending to one grade. Unclassified",
              "sessions are not drawn. Counts Cowork sessions only; follows a grade clicked on the WHAT chart. SVG",
              "image URL (dataCategory ImageUrl); the ? is percent-encoded (%3F) like the # of the colours (%23), and",
              "widths are whole pixels so no locale decimal separator can break the image."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _H = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Strong fit\")), 0)",
              "VAR _M = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Fair fit\")), 0)",
              "VAR _L = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Worth a look\")), 0)",
              "VAR _n = _H + _M + _L",
              "VAR _kinds = INT(_H > 0) + INT(_M > 0) + INT(_L > 0)",
              "VAR _g = SWITCH(TRUE(), _H > 0, \"S\", _M > 0, \"F\", \"%3F\")",
              "VAR _fill = SWITCH(_g, \"S\", \"%2309B39D\", \"F\", \"%23F6A392\", \"%23B11F4B\")",
              "VAR _ink = IF(_g = \"F\", \"%231C2632\", \"%23FFFFFF\")",
              "VAR _dot =",
              "    \"<circle cx='30' cy='10' r='9' fill='\" & _fill & \"'/>\"",
              "        & \"<text x='30' y='14' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif' font-size='11' font-weight='700' fill='\"",
              "        & _ink & \"'>\" & _g & \"</text>\"",
              "VAR _b1 = ROUND(56 * DIVIDE(_H, _n), 0)",
              "VAR _b2 = ROUND(56 * DIVIDE(_H + _M, _n), 0)",
              "VAR _bar =",
              "    \"<defs><clipPath id='c'><rect x='2' y='5' width='56' height='10' rx='5'/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path='url(%23c)'>\"",
              "        & IF(_b1 > 0, \"<rect x='2' y='5' width='\" & FORMAT(_b1, \"0\") & \"' height='10' fill='%2309B39D'/>\")",
              "        & IF(_b2 > _b1, \"<rect x='\" & FORMAT(2 + _b1, \"0\") & \"' y='5' width='\" & FORMAT(_b2 - _b1, \"0\") & \"' height='10' fill='%23F6A392'/>\")",
              "        & IF(_b2 < 56, \"<rect x='\" & FORMAT(2 + _b2, \"0\") & \"' y='5' width='\" & FORMAT(56 - _b2, \"0\") & \"' height='10' fill='%23B11F4B'/>\")",
              "        & \"</g>\"",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        _n > 0,",
              "        \"data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='60' height='20' viewBox='0 0 60 20'>\"",
              "            & IF(_kinds = 1, _dot, _bar) & \"</svg>\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000016",
            "dataCategory": "ImageUrl"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Usage Share",
            "description": [
              "Tooltip on the ranked MODEL USAGE chart: a model's sessions as a share of all sessions in the selection.",
              "A session that used two models counts under both, so the bars can add to a little over 100% (typically by",
              "around 2%). \"Embedded App (no model logged)\"",
              "is kept as a bar on purpose - it is the Not judged base, shown rather than hidden."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "DIVIDE(",
              "    [Model: Sessions],",
              "    CALCULATE([Model: Sessions], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AI_Model], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Model Cost Tier], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Model Cost Tier Sort]))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000018"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: High Fit Share",
            "description": [
              "STRONG FIT % on the Cowork Fit KPI row: Strong-fit Cowork sessions as a share of graded sessions",
              "(unclassified sessions are outside the base, so Strong + Fair + Worth a look = 100%)."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "DIVIDE(",
              "    CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Strong fit\")),",
              "    [Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks]",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0%",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000019"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Low Fit Share",
            "description": [
              "WORTH A LOOK % on the Cowork Fit KPI row: Cowork sessions graded Worth a look (at Balanced grading,",
              "chat where nothing was read or attached) as a share of graded sessions."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Usage Efficiency: Low Fit Tasks], [Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks])",
            "formatString": "0%",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-00000000001a"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Task Grade Share",
            "description": [
              "WHAT chart on Cowork Fit: the share of a task's graded Cowork sessions that fell in the grade in context,",
              "so each task's bar splits into Strong / Fair / Worth a look and adds to 100%. Fit is graded per session, so one",
              "task holds all three grades. The grade is removed from the base only; the task, organisation and date",
              "filters stay. Unclassified sessions return blank."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "DIVIDE(",
              "    CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] IN {\"Strong fit\", \"Fair fit\", \"Worth a look\"})),",
              "    CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]))",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "0%",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-00000000001b"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Who Graded Sessions",
            "description": [
              "WHO table on Cowork Fit: graded Cowork sessions for the organisation or person, across all three grades",
              "(a grade clicked on the WHAT chart does not narrow it - the row shows its whole mix). Blank below 5",
              "graded sessions, so one-off users do not top a share ranking; the matrix hides those rows."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _n = CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]))",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(_n >= 5, _n)"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-00000000001c"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Who People",
            "description": [
              "WHO table on Cowork Fit: people in the organisation with 5+ graded Cowork sessions (the rows shown when",
              "it is expanded). Blank on a person row."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _u =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] IN {\"Strong fit\", \"Fair fit\", \"Worth a look\"}),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\")",
              "    )",
              "VAR _p = COUNTROWS(FILTER(_u, CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Graded Tasks], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort])) >= 5))",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(NOT ISINSCOPE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]) && NOT ISBLANK([Usage Efficiency: Who Graded Sessions]), _p)"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-00000000001d"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Who High Share",
            "description": "WHO table: Strong-fit share of the row's graded Cowork sessions (5+ graded only).",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _n = [Usage Efficiency: Who Graded Sessions]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        NOT ISBLANK(_n),",
              "        DIVIDE(CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Strong fit\"), _n) + 0",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0%",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-00000000001e"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Who Medium Share",
            "description": "WHO table: Fair-fit share of the row's graded Cowork sessions (5+ graded only).",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _n = [Usage Efficiency: Who Graded Sessions]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        NOT ISBLANK(_n),",
              "        DIVIDE(CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Fair fit\"), _n) + 0",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0%",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-00000000001f"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Who Low Share",
            "description": [
              "WHO table: Worth-a-look share of the row's graded Cowork sessions (5+ graded only). The table's sort:",
              "the people and teams whose Cowork sessions most often show no sign Cowork was needed - a coaching",
              "prompt, not a ranking."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _n = [Usage Efficiency: Who Graded Sessions]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        NOT ISBLANK(_n),",
              "        DIVIDE(CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Worth a look\"), _n) + 0",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0%",
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000020"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Who Mix",
            "description": [
              "WHO table: the row's Strong / Fair / Worth a look mix as one bar (teal / coral / crimson, the fit chart colours),",
              "so a team or person reads as a mix, not a single grade. SVG image URL; whole-pixel widths so no locale",
              "decimal separator can break the image. Blank below 5 graded sessions."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _n = [Usage Efficiency: Who Graded Sessions]",
              "VAR _H = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Strong fit\"), 0)",
              "VAR _M = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Usage Efficiency: Consumption Sessions], REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]), 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade] = \"Fair fit\"), 0)",
              "VAR _b1 = ROUND(116 * DIVIDE(_H, _n), 0)",
              "VAR _b2 = ROUND(116 * DIVIDE(_H + _M, _n), 0)",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        NOT ISBLANK(_n),",
              "        \"data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='120' height='20' viewBox='0 0 120 20'>\"",
              "            & \"<defs><clipPath id='c'><rect x='2' y='5' width='116' height='10' rx='5'/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path='url(%23c)'>\"",
              "            & IF(_b1 > 0, \"<rect x='2' y='5' width='\" & FORMAT(_b1, \"0\") & \"' height='10' fill='%2309B39D'/>\")",
              "            & IF(_b2 > _b1, \"<rect x='\" & FORMAT(2 + _b1, \"0\") & \"' y='5' width='\" & FORMAT(_b2 - _b1, \"0\") & \"' height='10' fill='%23F6A392'/>\")",
              "            & IF(_b2 < 116, \"<rect x='\" & FORMAT(2 + _b2, \"0\") & \"' y='5' width='\" & FORMAT(116 - _b2, \"0\") & \"' height='10' fill='%23B11F4B'/>\")",
              "            & \"</g></svg>\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000021",
            "dataCategory": "ImageUrl"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Efficiency: Who Flag",
            "description": [
              "WHO table flag: marks a person with 5+ graded Cowork sessions of which half or more were graded",
              "Worth a look - a coaching prompt, not a verdict. On an organisation or total row it shows how many",
              "people in it are flagged. Reads Who Low Share, so it always agrees with the table's own column,",
              "and ignores a grade clicked on the WHAT chart, like the rest of the table."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _people =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]),",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade], 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Weight Grade Sort]),",
              "        KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Agent Filter (Normalized)] = \"Cowork\")",
              "    )",
              "VAR _flagged = COUNTROWS(FILTER(_people, [Usage Efficiency: Who Low Share] >= 0.5))",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        _flagged > 0,",
              "        IF(ISINSCOPE('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Audit_UserId]), \"⚑\", \"⚑ \" & FORMAT(_flagged, \"0\"))",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Usage Efficiency",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000e1-0000-0000-0000-000000000002"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Judged Share",
            "description": [
              "\"Judged\" column on the Model Fit table: share of the row's sessions that model fit can speak to (model",
              "logged and work graded). The Good / Lighter model may do / Try stronger columns are shares of THIS base."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Model: Judged Sessions], [Model: Sessions])",
            "formatString": "0%",
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000022"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Verdict Icon",
            "description": [
              "VERDICT icon on the Model Fit table: the most common outcome among the row's judged sessions - teal tick",
              "= Good match, crimson down arrow = Lighter model may do, orange up arrow = Try stronger (ties go to Good match,",
              "then Lighter model may do). Grey dash under 5 judged sessions. Glyphs are SVG paths (no font dependency); image URL."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _s = [Model: Sessions]",
              "VAR _j = COALESCE([Model: Judged Sessions], 0)",
              "VAR _c = COALESCE([Model: Over-specified Sessions], 0)",
              "VAR _u = COALESCE([Model: Under-specified Sessions], 0)",
              "VAR _g = _j - _c - _u",
              "VAR _v = SWITCH(TRUE(), _j < 5, \"N\", _g >= _c && _g >= _u, \"G\", _c >= _u, \"C\", \"S\")",
              "VAR _fill = SWITCH(_v, \"G\", \"%2309B39D\", \"C\", \"%23B11F4B\", \"S\", \"%23F1963A\", \"%23C8CDD4\")",
              "VAR _path =",
              "    SWITCH(",
              "        _v,",
              "        \"G\", \"M25.5 10.5 L28.5 13.5 L34.5 7\",",
              "        \"C\", \"M30 5.5 V14.5 M26.5 11 L30 14.5 L33.5 11\",",
              "        \"S\", \"M30 14.5 V5.5 M26.5 9 L30 5.5 L33.5 9\",",
              "        \"M26 10 H34\"",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        COALESCE(_s, 0) > 0,",
              "        \"data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='60' height='20' viewBox='0 0 60 20'>\"",
              "            & \"<circle cx='30' cy='10' r='9' fill='\" & _fill & \"'/>\"",
              "            & \"<path d='\" & _path & \"' fill='none' stroke='%23FFFFFF' stroke-width='2.2' stroke-linecap='round' stroke-linejoin='round'/></svg>\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000023",
            "dataCategory": "ImageUrl"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Main Model",
            "description": [
              "\"Main model\" on the Model Fit table: the row's most-used logged model (name trimmed at its first bracket)",
              "and its share of the row's logged session x model pairs. \"Embedded App (no model logged)\" is excluded."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _t =",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        ADDCOLUMNS(VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AI_Model]), \"@n\", [Model: Sessions]),",
              "        NOT ISBLANK('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AI_Model]) && LEFT('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AI_Model], 8) <> \"Embedded\" && [@n] > 0",
              "    )",
              "VAR _tot = SUMX(_t, [@n])",
              "VAR _top = TOPN(1, _t, [@n], DESC, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AI_Model], ASC)",
              "VAR _nm = MAXX(_top, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[AI_Model])",
              "VAR _cut = SEARCH(\" (\", _nm, 1, 0)",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        _tot > 0,",
              "        IF(_cut > 0, LEFT(_nm, _cut - 1), _nm) & \" · \" & FORMAT(DIVIDE(MAXX(_top, [@n]), _tot), \"0%\")",
              "    )"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000024"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Main Reason",
            "description": [
              "\"Main reason\" on the Model Fit table: the work shape (\"how it was done\") most common among the row's",
              "Lighter model may do and Try stronger sessions, with its share of them. Blank when nothing is flagged."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _t =",
              "    FILTER(",
              "        ADDCOLUMNS(",
              "            VALUES('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Shape]),",
              "            \"@n\", COALESCE([Model: Over-specified Sessions], 0) + COALESCE([Model: Under-specified Sessions], 0)",
              "        ),",
              "        [@n] > 0",
              "    )",
              "VAR _tot = SUMX(_t, [@n])",
              "VAR _top = TOPN(1, _t, [@n], DESC, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Shape], ASC)",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(_tot > 0, MAXX(_top, 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Work Shape]) & \" · \" & FORMAT(DIVIDE(MAXX(_top, [@n]), _tot), \"0%\"))"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000025"
          },
          {
            "name": "Model: Fit Table Title",
            "description": [
              "Title of the Model Fit table, following the Show-by buttons (field parameter 'Model Fit View').",
              "Reads the hidden Order column: DAX cannot read a field parameter's display column, which is part of a",
              "composite key with its Fields column (\"not all columns of the composite key are included\")."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR _o = SELECTEDVALUE('Model Fit View'[Model Fit View Order], 0)",
              "RETURN",
              "    \"MODEL FIT BY \" & SWITCH(_o, 1, \"ORGANISATION\", 2, \"PERSON\", \"TASK\")"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "Model Mix",
            "lineageTag": "fc0000d1-0000-0000-0000-000000000026"
          },
          {
            "name": "Usage Rows",
            "expression": "CALCULATE(COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'), KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Usage Row] = TRUE()))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "isHidden": true,
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Overall - Value",
            "description": [
              "Prompt rows plus Cowork scheduled-run task rows. The basis for the",
              "active-user counts, so someone whose only Copilot use was a scheduled",
              "Cowork run still counts as active. Not a prompt count: use AI Tasks."
            ],
            "lineageTag": "42080893-2fee-5720-8a9c-285afbff1b6f"
          },
          {
            "name": "Cowork Scheduled Runs",
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    COUNTROWS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'),",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is_Cowork] = TRUE()),",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[Is Prompt Row] = FALSE())",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "AI Fluency\\Cowork - Value",
            "description": [
              "Scheduled or autonomous Cowork runs: Cowork audit records with no user",
              "prompt, kept as one task row each. Not counted in AI Tasks or AI Prompts."
            ],
            "lineageTag": "a75606cb-fe09-5210-bc87-8ce904c615b8"
          }
        ],
        "hierarchies": [
          {
            "name": "Value_Outcome Hierarchy",
            "lineageTag": "32c2c649-b74e-4956-bff7-559d24a67fd9",
            "levels": [
              {
                "name": "Value_Outcome",
                "ordinal": 0,
                "column": "Value_Outcome",
                "lineageTag": "97e316e7-d38e-4173-bae1-33318dff2696"
              },
              {
                "name": "Behavior",
                "ordinal": 1,
                "column": "Behavior_Enriched_Full",
                "lineageTag": "c1d964dc-0f31-4e8e-b174-bc0b9fcd6e2d"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "annotations": [
          {
            "name": "PBI_ResultType",
            "value": "Table"
          },
          {
            "name": "PBI_NavigationStepName",
            "value": "Navigation"
          },
          {
            "name": "PBI_IsMQueryFoldable",
            "value": "True"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "Copilot Licensed",
        "lineageTag": "d2642023-4b65-422e-b87e-2db288a27359",
        "columns": [
          {
            "name": "User Principal Name",
            "dataType": "string",
            "sourceColumn": "User Principal Name",
            "lineageTag": "272d6b1b-4f26-4fcf-aedf-0b0bbbbe42a7",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "changedProperties": [
              {
                "property": "IsHidden"
              }
            ],
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "SummarizationSetBy",
                "value": "Automatic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "Has license",
            "dataType": "string",
            "sourceColumn": "Has license",
            "lineageTag": "71a5d25c-0ad3-4d0c-abf2-f2f75725fe21",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "changedProperties": [
              {
                "property": "IsHidden"
              }
            ],
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "SummarizationSetBy",
                "value": "Automatic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "UPN_Normalized",
            "dataType": "string",
            "sourceColumn": "UPN_Normalized",
            "lineageTag": "d34e7c05-021e-4f79-96db-dce2199ce840",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "SummarizationSetBy",
                "value": "Automatic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "calculated",
            "name": "Days Since Last Active",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "description": [
              "Days since the user was last active, measured to the AS-OF DATE = the last day of loaded audit",
              "data, not TODAY(). For a live tenant refreshed daily the two are the same, so production numbers",
              "are unchanged; for a fixed or lagging extract, anchoring to today would age every seat by the",
              "reporting lag and report the whole estate as dormant. Never-active licensed users (blank",
              "LastActiveDate) get the DATA WINDOW SPAN instead - the provable lower bound on how long they've",
              "been inactive (zero activity across the whole audit window). So with ~6 months of data a",
              "never-active seat reads as ~180 days and lands in the 180+ reclaim pocket; with a short window it",
              "stays small and the Dormancy Bucket labels it \"Never active\" rather than over-claiming 180+."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR WindowStart =",
              "    CALCULATE ( MIN ( 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate] ), ALL ( 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)' ) )",
              "VAR WindowEnd =",
              "    CALCULATE ( MAX ( 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate] ), ALL ( 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)' ) )",
              "VAR DataSpan = DATEDIFF ( WindowStart, WindowEnd, DAY )",
              "VAR AsOfDate = COALESCE ( WindowEnd, TODAY () )",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF (",
              "        ISBLANK ( 'Copilot Licensed'[LastActiveDate] ),",
              "        DataSpan,",
              "        MAX ( 0, DATEDIFF ( 'Copilot Licensed'[LastActiveDate], AsOfDate, DAY ) )",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-col-dayssince-0001",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "SummarizationSetBy",
                "value": "Automatic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "calculated",
            "name": "Dormancy Bucket",
            "dataType": "string",
            "description": [
              "Recency band for the dormancy column chart. Sorted via Dormancy Bucket Order.",
              "Never-active seats fold into the inactive band their data-window span supports (e.g. 180+ with",
              "~6 months of data); if the window is too short to prove even 30 days, they stay \"Never active\"."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR d = 'Copilot Licensed'[Days Since Last Active]",
              "VAR neverActive = ISBLANK ( 'Copilot Licensed'[LastActiveDate] )",
              "RETURN",
              "    SWITCH (",
              "        TRUE (),",
              "        neverActive, \"Never active\",",
              "        d < 30, \"Active (<30 days)\",",
              "        d < 90, \"Inactive 30-89 days\",",
              "        d < 180, \"Inactive 90-179 days\",",
              "        \"Inactive 180+ days\"",
              "    )"
            ],
            "sortByColumn": "Dormancy Bucket Order",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-col-bucket-0001",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "SummarizationSetBy",
                "value": "Automatic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "calculated",
            "name": "Dormancy Bucket Order",
            "dataType": "int64",
            "description": "Sort key so the dormancy buckets render in recency order, not alphabetically.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR d = 'Copilot Licensed'[Days Since Last Active]",
              "VAR neverActive = ISBLANK ( 'Copilot Licensed'[LastActiveDate] )",
              "RETURN",
              "    SWITCH (",
              "        TRUE (),",
              "        neverActive, 5,",
              "        d < 30, 1,",
              "        d < 90, 2,",
              "        d < 180, 3,",
              "        4",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "0",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-col-bucketorder-0001",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "SummarizationSetBy",
                "value": "Automatic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "calculated",
            "name": "LastActiveDate",
            "dataType": "dateTime",
            "description": [
              "Last Copilot activity date, DERIVED from the audit-log interactions: MAX(ActivityDate) per",
              "user via the audit -> Copilot Licensed[UPN_Normalized] relationship. Blank = never active in",
              "the period; those never-active licensed seats are still kept and attributed to their org."
            ],
            "expression": "CALCULATE ( MAX ( 'Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate] ) )",
            "formatString": "General Date",
            "lineageTag": "9a2936f7-fa1e-4bcc-9a38-9ff9b5a351da",
            "summarizeBy": "none",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "name": "SummarizationSetBy",
                "value": "Automatic"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "partitions": [
          {
            "name": "Copilot Licensed",
            "mode": "import",
            "source": {
              "type": "m",
              "expression": [
                "let",
                "\t\t\t\t    // Accepts a SharePoint URL (https://...) or a local file path (c:\\... or \\\\server\\...).",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"Promoted Headers\" = Table.Buffer(FabricTable(\"copilot_licensed_users\")),  // Table.Buffer breaks query folding so missing-column guards below work on customers whose file has only User Principal Name + Has License",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    // List accepted variants for User Principal Name",
                "\t\t\t\t    userPrincipalNameVariants = {\"User Principal Name\", \"userPrincipalName\", \"UserPrincipalName\", \"User principal name\", \"User_Principal_Name\"},",
                "\t\t\t\t    actualUPNColumn = List.First(List.Intersect({userPrincipalNameVariants, Table.ColumnNames(#\"Promoted Headers\")}), null),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    // List accepted variants for Has License",
                "\t\t\t\t    hasLicenseVariants = {",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"Has license\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"Has License\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"HasLicense\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"HasCopilot\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"Has Copilot\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"Has Copilot License\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"Has Copilot license\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"HasCopilotLicense\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"Has Copilot License Assigned\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"Has Copilot license assigned\",",
                "\t\t\t\t        \"isUser\",",
                "                \"Has_license\"",
                "\t\t\t\t    },",
                "\t\t\t\t    actualHasLicenseColumn = List.First(List.Intersect({hasLicenseVariants, Table.ColumnNames(#\"Promoted Headers\")}), null),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    // Add missing columns with defaults if not found, then rename",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"With UPN\" = if actualUPNColumn <> null then",
                "\t\t\t\t            #\"Promoted Headers\"",
                "\t\t\t\t        else",
                "\t\t\t\t            Table.AddColumn(#\"Promoted Headers\", \"User Principal Name\", each null, type text),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"With License\" = if actualHasLicenseColumn <> null then",
                "\t\t\t\t            #\"With UPN\"",
                "\t\t\t\t        else",
                "\t\t\t\t            Table.AddColumn(#\"With UPN\", \"Has license\", each \"Unknown\", type text),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"Renamed Columns\" =",
                "\t\t\t\t        Table.RenameColumns(",
                "\t\t\t\t            #\"With License\",",
                "\t\t\t\t            List.Combine({",
                "\t\t\t\t                if actualUPNColumn <> null and actualUPNColumn <> \"User Principal Name\" then {{actualUPNColumn, \"User Principal Name\"}} else {},",
                "\t\t\t\t                if actualHasLicenseColumn <> null and actualHasLicenseColumn <> \"Has license\" then {{actualHasLicenseColumn, \"Has license\"}} else {}",
                "\t\t\t\t            }),",
                "\t\t\t\t            MissingField.Ignore",
                "\t\t\t\t        ),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    // Add a normalized join key (case-insensitive match helper).",
                "\t\t\t\t    // Idempotent: if the source Delta table already has UPN_Normalized",
                "\t\t\t\t    // (older pre-normalized ingester output), keep it instead of re-adding.",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"Added UPN Normalized\" =",
                "\t\t\t\t        if Table.HasColumns(#\"Renamed Columns\", \"UPN_Normalized\") then",
                "\t\t\t\t            #\"Renamed Columns\"",
                "\t\t\t\t        else",
                "\t\t\t\t            Table.AddColumn(",
                "\t\t\t\t                #\"Renamed Columns\",",
                "\t\t\t\t                \"UPN_Normalized\",",
                "\t\t\t\t                each",
                "\t\t\t\t                    let v = [User Principal Name]",
                "\t\t\t\t                    in if v = null then null else Text.Lower(Text.Trim(Text.From(v))),",
                "\t\t\t\t                type text",
                "\t\t\t\t            ),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    // Remove duplicates using the normalized key",
                "\t\t\t\t    // ROBUSTNESS: a customer licensed-users export can contain a row with a missing",
                "\t\t\t\t    // User Principal Name. UPN_Normalized is a relationship key (one side) and cannot be blank,",
                "\t\t\t\t    // so drop null/empty-UPN rows (they cannot join to any fact anyway) before deduping.",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"Filtered Blank UPN\" = Table.SelectRows(#\"Added UPN Normalized\", each [UPN_Normalized] <> null and Text.Trim([UPN_Normalized]) <> \"\"),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"Removed Duplicates\" = Table.Distinct(#\"Filtered Blank UPN\", {\"UPN_Normalized\"}),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    // LastActiveDate is now a CALCULATED column derived from the audit logs (MAX ActivityDate per",
                "\t\t\t\t    // user). Drop any sourced LastActiveDate so it cannot clash with the calculated column.",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"Coerced LastActiveDate\" = Table.RemoveColumns(#\"Removed Duplicates\", {\"LastActiveDate\"}, MissingField.Ignore),",
                "",
                "\t\t\t\t    // ROBUSTNESS #1: UserId / DisplayName are OPTIONAL. Some licensed exports have only",
                "\t\t\t\t    // User Principal Name + Has License. Add as null when absent so the model columns",
                "\t\t\t\t    // (sourceColumn UserId / DisplayName) never error on customers without them.",
                "\t\t\t\t    #\"Ensure Optional Cols\" =",
                "\t\t\t\t        let",
                "\t\t\t\t            t0 = if Table.HasColumns(#\"Coerced LastActiveDate\", \"UserId\") then #\"Coerced LastActiveDate\" else Table.AddColumn(#\"Coerced LastActiveDate\", \"UserId\", each null, type text),",
                "\t\t\t\t            t1 = if Table.HasColumns(t0, \"DisplayName\") then t0 else Table.AddColumn(t0, \"DisplayName\", each null, type text)",
                "\t\t\t\t        in t1,",
                "\t\t\t\t    // Lean pass: drop source columns nothing in the model reads.",
                "\t\t\t\t    __lean = Table.RemoveColumns(#\"Ensure Optional Cols\", {\"UserId\", \"DisplayName\", \"Assigned_Products\", \"Deleted_Date\", \"Display_Name\", \"Exchange_Last_Activity_Date\", \"Exchange_License_Assign_Date\", \"Has_Exchange_License\", \"Has_OneDrive_License\", \"Has_SharePoint_License\", \"Has_Skype_For_Business_License\", \"Has_Teams_License\", \"Has_Yammer_License\", \"Is_Deleted\", \"OneDrive_Last_Activity_Date\", \"OneDrive_License_Assign_Date\", \"Report_Refresh_Date\", \"SharePoint_Last_Activity_Date\", \"SharePoint_License_Assign_Date\", \"Skype_For_Business_Last_Activity_Date\", \"Skype_For_Business_License_Assign_Date\", \"Teams_Last_Activity_Date\", \"Teams_License_Assign_Date\", \"Yammer_Last_Activity_Date\", \"Yammer_License_Assign_Date\"}, MissingField.Ignore)",
                "\t\t\t\tin",
                "\t\t\t\t    __lean"
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "measures": [
          {
            "name": "Total Licensed Users",
            "description": [
              "Total licensed users count (deduped on UPN_Normalized).",
              "Re-used by Inactive Licensed Users + Licensed Utilisation %."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "CALCULATE(",
              "    DISTINCTCOUNT('Copilot Licensed'[UPN_Normalized]),",
              "    UPPER(TRIM('Copilot Licensed'[Has license])) IN {\"YES\",\"TRUE\",\"Y\",\"1\"}",
              ")"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "% Active Licensed Users",
            "description": "License utilization is unavailable if the roster cannot be reconciled or active users exceed matched license holders.",
            "expression": "VAR _Total = [Licensed Users (Filter-Aware)] VAR _Active = [Active Licensed Users] RETURN IF(_Total > 0 && _Active <= _Total, DIVIDE(_Active, _Total))",
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000015"
          },
          {
            "name": "% Active Unlicensed Users",
            "description": "Unlicensed active share only when inventory and observed activity reconcile.",
            "expression": "VAR _Total = [Unlicensed Users (Filter-Aware)] VAR _Active = [Active Unlicensed Users] RETURN IF(_Total > 0 && _Active <= _Total, DIVIDE(_Active, _Total))",
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000016"
          },
          {
            "name": "Total Users (Filter-Aware)",
            "description": [
              "Total user population for the current filter context (Date, Organization slicer,",
              "axis department, etc). Built from 'Chat + Agent Org Data' so the Department dimension",
              "flows through naturally. This is the denominator for all \"(of Total)\" share measures."
            ],
            "expression": "DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Org Data'[PersonId_Normalized])",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000020"
          },
          {
            "name": "Licensed Users (Filter-Aware)",
            "description": [
              "Licensed users respecting the current Department / Org filter context.",
              "Uses TREATAS to virtually relate Copilot Licensed[UPN_Normalized] to",
              "Org Data[PersonId_Normalized] so a Department slicer correctly restricts",
              "the licensed population (no physical relationship exists between the two)."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "VAR LicensedUPNs =",
              "    CALCULATETABLE(",
              "        VALUES('Copilot Licensed'[UPN_Normalized]),",
              "        UPPER(TRIM('Copilot Licensed'[Has license])) IN {\"YES\",\"TRUE\",\"Y\",\"1\"},",
              "        REMOVEFILTERS('Chat + Agent Org Data')",
              "    )",
              "RETURN",
              "    CALCULATE(",
              "        DISTINCTCOUNT('Chat + Agent Org Data'[PersonId_Normalized]),",
              "        TREATAS(LicensedUPNs, 'Chat + Agent Org Data'[PersonId_Normalized])",
              "    )"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000021"
          },
          {
            "name": "Unlicensed Users (Filter-Aware)",
            "description": "Matched organizational population less matched licensed population, only when license inventory reconciles. Missing or inconsistent inventory is not zero.",
            "expression": [
              "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 1,",
              "(VAR _Total = [Total Users (Filter-Aware)] VAR _Licensed = [Licensed Users (Filter-Aware)] RETURN IF(NOT ISBLANK(_Licensed) && _Licensed <= _Total, _Total - _Licensed)))"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000022"
          },
          {
            "name": "Inactive Licensed Users (Filter-Aware)",
            "description": "Inactive matched license holders; unavailable rather than negative when sources do not reconcile.",
            "expression": "VAR _Total = [Licensed Users (Filter-Aware)] VAR _Active = [Active Licensed Users] RETURN IF(NOT ISBLANK(_Total) && _Active <= _Total, _Total - COALESCE(_Active,0))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000023"
          },
          {
            "name": "Inactive Unlicensed Users (Filter-Aware)",
            "description": "Inactive unlicensed users only when the source populations reconcile.",
            "expression": "VAR _Total = [Unlicensed Users (Filter-Aware)] VAR _Active = [Active Unlicensed Users] RETURN IF(NOT ISBLANK(_Total) && _Active <= _Total, _Total - COALESCE(_Active,0))",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "Activation",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000024"
          },
          {
            "name": "% Active Unlicensed Users (of Total)",
            "description": "% of all users in the current filter context who are active unlicensed chat users.",
            "expression": "DIVIDE([Active Unlicensed Users], [Total Users (Filter-Aware)], 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000026"
          },
          {
            "name": "% Active Users (of Total)",
            "description": [
              "% of all users (in current filter context) who are active in any capacity.",
              "Filter-aware on Date, Organization, axis Department, usage-rank slicers."
            ],
            "expression": "DIVIDE([All Active Users], [Total Users (Filter-Aware)], 0)",
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000041"
          },
          {
            "name": "% Active Users Using Agents",
            "description": [
              "% of all users (in current filter context) who interacted with at least one agent.",
              "Numerator is [Active Agent Users] (alias of [Active Agent Users] on Audit Logs);",
              "denominator is the filter-aware Org Data spine, so this responds to Date, Organization,",
              "axis Department, and the usage-rank slicers."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    DIVIDE([Active Agent Users], [All Active Users], 0)",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-0001-0001-0001-000000000042"
          },
          {
            "name": "Using Copilot / Not Using Agents",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    MAX(0, [All Active Users] - [Active Agent Users])",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "2dcc8e65-00bf-4314-8f20-a63486fd7394"
          },
          {
            "name": "% Inactive Users (of Total)",
            "description": "How to read: lower is better by definition. Use the Internal Benchmark to see which orgs sit worse than the tenant as a whole.",
            "expression": [
              "",
              "    DIVIDE([Inactive Users (Filter-Aware)], [Total Users (Filter-Aware)], 0)",
              ""
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness",
            "lineageTag": "1305efc5-94b7-4630-bc84-0611429f17a9"
          },
          {
            "name": "Licensed Inactive 30d+",
            "description": [
              "=== DORMANCY (last-activity recency) ============================================",
              "Days since the user was last active (from LastActiveDate to today). Live: recomputes",
              "against TODAY(), not pinned to the export date. Blank LastActiveDate = never active."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 1,",
              "(CALCULATE(",
              "    DISTINCTCOUNT('Copilot Licensed'[UPN_Normalized]),",
              "    UPPER(TRIM('Copilot Licensed'[Has license])) IN {\"YES\",\"TRUE\",\"Y\",\"1\"},",
              "    'Copilot Licensed'[Days Since Last Active] >= 30",
              ")))"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness\\Dormancy",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-dorm-0001-000000000001"
          },
          {
            "name": "Days Since Last Active (Value)",
            "description": [
              "Days since last active as a MEASURE so it can sit in a table's Values without Power BI",
              "forcing a count (a 'don't summarize' column shows 1 per row). One row per user, so MAX = the user's value."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 1,",
              "(MAX('Copilot Licensed'[Days Since Last Active])))"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness\\Dormancy",
            "lineageTag": "cc010001-dorm-0001-000000000009"
          },
          {
            "name": "Avg Days Since Last Active",
            "expression": [
              "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 1,",
              "(",
              "AVERAGEX (",
              "    VALUES ( 'Copilot Licensed'[User Principal Name] ),",
              "    [Days Since Last Active (Value)]",
              ")",
              "))"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0",
            "lineageTag": "f8f85a3a-0257-4de9-acb9-cf4d1aa39e7f"
          },
          {
            "name": "License Evidence Notice",
            "description": [
              "Plain-language statement of how far the dormancy thresholds can actually be",
              "evidenced. 'Days Since Last Active' is good-fit to the audit window, not to",
              "today, so a threshold longer than the window cannot be distinguished from a",
              "never-active seat. Put this on the page so the dormancy cards are read honestly."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 0, \"License inventory does not reconcile to the organizational roster and observed licensed users. Dormancy and reclaim estimates are unavailable until identity/license mapping is corrected.\",",
              "(VAR FirstDay = CALCULATE(MIN('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]), ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'))",
              "VAR LastDay = CALCULATE(MAX('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[InteractionDate]), ALL('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'))",
              "VAR SpanDays = DATEDIFF(FirstDay, LastDay, DAY)",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        ISBLANK(FirstDay),",
              "        \"No audit activity is loaded, so dormancy cannot be assessed.\",",
              "        \"Dormancy is measured against the audit window (\" & FORMAT(FirstDay, \"d MMM yyyy\") & \" to \" & FORMAT(LastDay, \"d MMM yyyy\") & \", \" & SpanDays & \" days), not against today. \"",
              "            & IF(",
              "                SpanDays < 90,",
              "                \"The window is shorter than 90 days, so a never-active seat reads as roughly \" & SpanDays & \" days dormant and the 90d+ and 180d+ cuts cannot be evidenced. Treat 30d+ as 'no activity in the loaded window', not as a confirmed reclaim list.\",",
              "                \"Thresholds longer than \" & SpanDays & \" days cannot be distinguished from a never-active seat.\"",
              "            )",
              "    )))"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness\\Dormancy",
            "lineageTag": "d459945b-4704-4870-aa5c-f7e2e6f5ce27"
          },
          {
            "name": "Reclaim Cost Notice",
            "description": [
              "States whether the reclaim figure is actually costed. Reclaimable cost is",
              "dormant seats multiplied by the Monthly Licence Cost parameter, so it reads",
              "zero until somebody sets that parameter - which otherwise looks like a bug."
            ],
            "expression": [
              "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 0, \"Reclaim value is unavailable until license inventory reconciles - see the dormancy evidence note.\",",
              "(VAR Cost = [Monthly Licence Cost Value]",
              "RETURN",
              "    IF(",
              "        Cost > 0,",
              "        \"Costed at \" & [Currency Symbol Value] & FORMAT(Cost, \"#,0\") & \" per licence per month (Monthly Licence Cost assumption).\",",
              "        \"Not costed: the Monthly Licence Cost assumption is 0, so the reclaimable value reads as zero. Set it in the model's Assumptions table to price the dormant seats.\"",
              "    )))"
            ],
            "displayFolder": "License Readiness\\Dormancy",
            "lineageTag": "ad35c9ec-82e3-4ede-9038-f492be2e1047"
          },
          {
            "name": "License Inventory Usable",
            "description": "One only when matched licensed roster is nonempty and accommodates observed licensed users. Ignores license-row/dormancy filters while respecting report date and organization context.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _Inventory = CALCULATE([Licensed Users (Filter-Aware)], REMOVEFILTERS('Copilot Licensed'))",
              "VAR _Active = CALCULATE([Active Licensed Users], REMOVEFILTERS('Copilot Licensed'))",
              "RETURN IF(_Inventory > 0 && _Active <= _Inventory, 1, 0)"
            ],
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Evidence",
            "lineageTag": "4874a0c6-b02b-4d42-af13-7a08f3c4db44"
          },
          {
            "name": "Unlicensed Share of Active Users",
            "description": "Prompt-active unlicensed users divided by all prompt-active users in the current context, not divided by license inventory.",
            "expression": [
              "VAR _Unlicensed = CALCULATE(",
              "    [All Active Users],",
              "    KEEPFILTERS('Chat + Agent Interactions (Audit Logs)'[License Status] = \"Unlicensed\"))",
              "RETURN DIVIDE(COALESCE(_Unlicensed, 0), [All Active Users])"
            ],
            "formatString": "0.0%",
            "displayFolder": "License Evidence",
            "lineageTag": "970ef66e-0a6d-4122-b85c-a1dbedfdddbc"
          },
          {
            "name": "Licensed Seats by Dormancy (Verified)",
            "description": "Source license rows by dormancy only when identity/license inventory is usable. Missing mapping is unavailable, not an inactive-user count.",
            "expression": "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 1, [Total Licensed Users])",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Evidence",
            "lineageTag": "ea6503e7-ba2c-47c8-afb5-d1816e5eaa5c"
          },
          {
            "name": "Active Licensed Users (Verified Inventory)",
            "description": "Active licensed users for inventory composition charts only. Blank when the inventory does not reconcile; the audit-based active-user KPI remains available.",
            "expression": "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 1, [Active Licensed Users])",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Evidence",
            "lineageTag": "32cc1056-ce41-40f2-be85-f7bdc88c155f"
          },
          {
            "name": "Active Unlicensed Users (Verified Inventory)",
            "description": "Active unlicensed users for inventory composition charts only. Blank when the licensed inventory cannot support a reliable unlicensed denominator.",
            "expression": "IF([License Inventory Usable] = 1, [Active Unlicensed Users])",
            "formatString": "#,##0",
            "displayFolder": "License Evidence",
            "lineageTag": "db0545d2-447f-4bfa-93a7-240a77a8bf23"
          }
        ],
        "annotations": [
          {
            "name": "PBI_NavigationStepName",
            "value": "Navigation"
          },
          {
            "name": "PBI_ResultType",
            "value": "Table"
          }
        ]
      },
